{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits","id":837712,"title":"Homebrew Embeds and Exploits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-26T12:32:22-08:00","id":837712,"title":"Homebrew Embeds and Exploits","content":"Similar to my Merit thread, this forum will be a hub for any homebrew material for Demon: The Descent. Specifically, for any Embeds and Exploits that allow for an Unchained to do something new.<br /> <br /> The main comment will be where I will put my master list of all the contributions here. At least, until I have a working GDoc. Until then, enjoy sharing your ideas <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T13:07:58-08:00","id":837729,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Blink of the Eye</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Mundane)<br /> The Demon exploits quantum uncertainty to change their location from one unobserved spot to another.<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Dexterity + Athletics - the highest Wits present + the highest Angel Rank (if any)<br /> <b>Action</b>: Reflexive</span></span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Demon glitches out their movement, appearing in someone\u2019s view and provoking Compromise.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Demon fails to shift locations.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Demon \u201cvanishes\u201d from one spot to appear at another unobserved location within double their Speed + Successes (as if they ran there &quot;with a little help&quot;).</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Extra successes are their own reward.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Note</b>: This Embed can only be activated once per Turn [without provoking Compromise?].<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Great for scenes where a momentary break in line of sight leads to you disappearing. Such as a bus passing in front of you. Or the target you are chasing turning their head.]</span></span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Wait For It</u> (Instrumental)<br /> The Demon plays with the exact temporal relationship an event has with its cause, delaying it a few moments.<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Wits + Science - Highest Intelligence present<br /> <b>Action</b>: Reflexive</span></span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure</span></span></b>: The consequence seems like it was deferred... only to strike with more force the very next moment. (Treat the effect as if Ripple was applied to it, but both the initial effect and the repeat happen at the same time.)<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure</span></span></b>: Nothing happens. Well, whatever you were trying to delay <i>actually</i> happens.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success</span></span></b>: The consequence is delayed up to Successes in Turns, where upon it happens normally.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success</span></span></b>: The Demon can delay the consequence until the end of the current Scene <i>or</i> the Demon can choose when to have the event occur within the normal time frame.<br /> <b>Possible Modifiers</b>: Viewers know with confidence exactly when the result should occur (-1 to -5), Reaction could plausibly be delayed or non-existant (such as an uninspected grenade being a dud) (+1 to +5).<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Great for those scenes when you need a grenade or burning car to explode <i>not now</i>, or for impressing the plebs by having their booby-traps visibly go off too late to affect you while you stroll right past them, unconcerned.] <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Fate Entanglement</u><br /> The Demon is able to entangle the physical and metaphysical states between two targets, ensuring what happens to one, also happens to the other.<br /> <b>Example Prerequisites</b>: Shift Consequence, Remote Link-up<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Intelligence + Science + Primum - Stamina + Primum<br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 2 Aether</span></span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure</span></span></b>: The entanglement happens in whatever way would be least advantageous for the Demon, as determined by the Storyteller.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure</span></span></b>: Nothing happens, other than the standard Compromise check for using an Exploit.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success</span></span></b>: The Demon entangles two subjects, both of which must be within the Demon's view. What happens to one, also happens to the other (as per Shift Consequences) for the remainder of the Scene.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success</span></span></b>: The Demon manages to plait the destinies' of others together with ease. Up to Primum + 2 targets can all be entangled such that what happens to any one of them, happens to them all.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Basically an ongoing Shift Consequences. Can spread the pain when two enemies are entangled, spread the health/wealth when allies are bound, or use as leverage when entangling yourself to a target that wants to kill you.] <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Failure At Any Cost</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Cacophonic)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sometimes it is not enough for you to succeed - others must fail. Demons are skilled at skewing probability in their favor, and it's only a short step to skewing it <i>against</i> someone else.<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Wits + Science - Successes on the targeted roll<br /> <b>Action</b>: Reflexive</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Fails <i>and</i> the Demon takes a point of Lethal damage for their hubris.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: No effect upon the outcome of the targeted roll. </span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Demon retroactively causes the attempted action to <i>just</i><i> barely</i> fail (causing the Failure effect to occur instead of Success or Exceptional Success), but the Demon incurs a point of Lethal damage as probability backlashes upon them. </span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Demon manages to make their target fail, and only get a little headache or bruising (1 Bashing damage) for their efforts.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[Comments: Mirror of </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Victory At Any Price</u>.]</span></span></span></span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Diagnostic</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Instrumental)<br /> The Demon can quickly determine a number of physical details about the target.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dice Roll</b>: Wits + Medicine for living creatures, Crafts for objects, Occult for other phenomena<br /> <b>Action</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Misleading information.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: No effect.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Demon can determine details such as Health, current physical Conditions, Durability, or Structure. One question can be asked per Success.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Details can include Physical Merits, Attribute dots, the general source of Conditions, and Equipment modifiers.<br /> <b>Possible Modifiers</b>: Target has strange and/or altered anatomy/structure (-1 to -5). Demon has never encountered the target's like before (-3). Target is supernaturally obscured or shielded (-1 to -5).</span></span></span></span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Knowledge Indexing</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Instrumental)<br /> The Demon can access and assess a person\u2019s \u201cpersonal index\u201d of known talents and knowledge. Not enough for mind reading, perhaps, but enough to get a general profile of their abilities. Note - this only covers knowledge and incidents the target is aware of; mental manipulation can cover or remove certain bits of information.<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Manipulation + Investigation - Composure + Primum<br /> <b>Action</b>: Reflexive</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Misleading information is provided instead.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: No effect.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Demon can determine details such as Skills, Specialties, and Mental and Social Merits. Each success lets the Demon ask one of the following questions:</span></span></span></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What is the target\u2019s highest skill(s)?</span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What is the target unskilled in?</span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What are the target\u2019s ranks in X skill? </span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Does the target have X speciality?</span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Does the target have X merit?</span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Whom does X merit pertain to?</span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Did the target use X skill/specialty/merit (within Primum days)?</span></span></span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Demon can access a greater degree of the person\u2019s self-knowledge. This can now include Virtue, Vice, or their equivalents. Allowable questions now include:</span></span></span></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Any of the previous questions, but timespan is now up to 1 month per Primum into the past.</span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What was the context of the last use of skill/specialty/merit X (within the past month)?</span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Has the target used skill/specialty/merit X in Y way within the past month?</span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What times did the target use X skill/specialty/merit in the past month?</span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Did the target\u2019s Integrity change in the past (Primum days)?</span></span></span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Note</b>: Each additional use of this Embed against the same target within the same day incurs a cumulative -1 penalty.</span></span></span></span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Mundana Obscura</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By use of this exploit, the Demon fades into the background, not becoming invisible so much as utterly beneath notice, just an expected part of the scenery. Additionally, the Demon can determine when the charade is in danger by detecting the ripples caused by direct attention and observation.</span></span><br /> <b>Example Prerequisites</b>: <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Authorized, Lost in the Crowd, Unperson, Occam\u2019s Razor</span></span><br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Presence + Subterfuge + Primum vs. Wits + Composure<br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant and Contested<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1 Aether<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dramatic Failure</b>: The Exploit backfires and </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>draws</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> attention instead of deflecting it. The Demon gains -5 to Stealth rolls until the end of scene.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The exploit fails and the world remains in full color.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Everything fades into grayscale until the end of the scene, and all others assume the Demon is just another expected part of the scene, unworthy of note or attention. Dramatically unusual actions, or particularly astute (or paranoid) sentries can jeopardize this concealment - the more attention that is paid to the Demon, the more color bleeds back into the source of the scrutiny. Note that observers still remember there was </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>someone</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> at the scene, just that they were supposed to be there. Even remote observation is affected - those viewing the Demon through cameras or clairvoyance are equally likely to ignore their presence. Historical information is <i>not</i> affected, however - someone else looking at photos or recordings of the scene will not be so quick to explain away the Demon's presence once the Exploit has expired.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success</b>: As success above, with an additional -5 to Perception or Clash of Wills rolls to detect the Demon. Additionally, observers quickly forget the Demon was ever there, and recorded media fails to accurately record the Demon's details.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Totally inspired by the potion/janitor scene in Fool Moon.]</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Stowaway</u><br /> Ghosts and Spirits often know how to anchor themselves to objects and even mortals. Even some angels can manage this, for when the God-Machine requires indirect, but constant monitoring of an asset. A few Demons have rediscovered this trick, pushing their Demonic Forms into Twilight, and tethering themselves to a target. Using this enable them to tail targets easily without their knowledge and might even let them bypass angelic security.<br /> <b>Example Prerequisites</b>: Tag and Release, Remote Link-up<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Presence + Stealth + Primum - Resolve + Primum<br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1 Aether</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Demon dematerializes and is bound to the target. They are unable to use Embeds, or spend Aether, until they make an extended Primum roll, with a target number equal to the target's Resolve or Durability, rolling once per hour.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Nothing happens, other than potentially drawing the Machine\u2019s attention for using an Exploit.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Unchained shifts to Twilight (Astral) and assumes Demonic Form. They are bound to remain near their target, as per the Fetter Manifestation, with the following exceptions: the Demon can Spoof to completely mask their presence inside the target (subject to Clash of Wills, as normal), and the Demon can utilize any Embeds they know, with the target being able to be treated as the source when applicable (allowing the Embeds to affect non-Twilight targets).</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Demon can now use Exploits through their target.</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> If the Demon ever fails a Compromise check, this Exploit immediately ends.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Great for smuggling yourself somewhere, or just &quot;haunting&quot; some unfortunate. Bear in mind that you Covers may degrade eventually due to neglect.]</span></span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>True Lies</u> (Vocal)<br /> The Demon can project their ability to determine the truth of their Cover's own statements upon others. Whatever lies the target utters, the Demon can force the target to believe that they are, in fact, actually truth. This Embed is ineffective when used on other Unchained.<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Manipulation + Empathy - Resolve<br /> <b>Action</b>: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dramatic Failure</b>: The Demon actually falls for what the target is saying and believes it is the actual truth.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Failure</b>: The target's perception of their own words remains unchanged.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Success</b>: The target now fully believes in what they said. Whether this is used to fortify a mortal accomplice's testimony (&quot;I really was at home with my friend last night&quot;), enforce their feigned declaration of loyalty (&quot;My only loyalty is to you, Dark One (and not the organization that sent me to spy on you)&quot;), or add weight to their half-hearted promises (&quot;Sure, I promise to pick you up whenever you need to&quot;), the subject fully feels that they were telling the truth and acts accordingly for the rest of the Scene.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success</b>: The subject is so committed to the &quot;truth&quot; that they reject all opposing evidence and resist changing their decision for Successes in days (maximum 1 week).</span></span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><u>Fuel Leak</u> (Cacophonic)<br /> Exploiting your half remembered knowledge of occult power flows, you sabotage another's access to their supernatural power source, causing them to slowly expend more than expected each time they tap it.<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Manipulation + Occult - Resolve + Primum<br /> <b>Action</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b>: The Demon sabotages their own Aether supplies and gains the Aetheric Bleed Condition.<br /> <b>Failure</b>: Nothing happens.<br /> <b>Success</b>: The target gains the Essence Leak (Mild) Condition, except it fades at the end of the Scene.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: Instead the target gains the Severe version of the Essence Leak Condition (though it, too, fades at the end of the Scene).<br /> <br /> [Condition] <u>Essence Leak (Mild)</u><br /> Your grasp on your source of power has been slackened. Whenever your lose a resource, such as Essence or Aether, be it through spending it or some other cause, you lose 1 additional point of it.<br /> <b>Possible Sources</b>: The Fuel Leak Embed. Using too much power beyond your normal limits. A curse.<br /> <b>Resolution</b>: Running out of Essence (or its equivalent).<br /> <b>Beat</b>: When the Condition resolves. If it fades before then, no Beat is acquired.<br /> [Storyteller's note: You may wish to keep the Condition hidden, so as to surprise the character when they reach for power and come up empty.]<br /> <br /> [Condition] <u>Essence Leak (Severe)</u><br /> As the mild form, except whenever you lose Essence or its equivalent, you lose double that amount instead.<br /> <br /> [<u>Comments</u>: This allows for some subtle screwing around with other supernaturals, or for a cunning Demon to trick their foes into emptying their reserves before a confrontation. It's up to the Storyteller if it affects things beyond Essence or Aether, though - Pyros or Mana seems easy enough, Vitae has some extra considerations, Pillars is very much an edge case, and Satiety is highly unlikely.]</span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><u>Aether Burn</u><br /> Tapping into your knowledge of occult power flows and conversions, your send a surge of unstable Aether into your target's power reserves, causing the Aether and it to mutually annihilate in a destructive manner. The Demon determines how much of their Aether they want to commit to this action when activating the Exploit (up to the maximum allowed for them to spend in 1 turn, as dictated by Primum and other factors).</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Example Prerequisites</b>: Fuel Leak, Combustion<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Intelligence + Occult + Primum - Resolve + Primum<br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1 or more Aether</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Demon screwed up the connection and backfires the Aether into themselves, losing additional Aether equal to what was spent and taking Lethal damage equal to the additional amount lost.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Aether bleeds into the void, doing nothing other than being lost.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The target loses Essence (or Aether, or another equivalent trait, per ST approval) for each Aether expended, and takes Lethal damage for each point of Essence (or equivalent) lost in this way.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Your Aether interacts in a particularly unstable manner. You can trade Lethal damage inflicted for Aggravated damage, on a 2-for-1 ratio (note, for some entities, this may result in additional Essence loss, which is separate but in addition to the base effect). Alternatively, if can inflict a Storyteller approved Condition or Tilt upon the target reflecting either internal damage, or problems with their power source.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>:This is what you break out when you need to stop those Angels from mauling you with their Numina. For crossover, it can also cause massive damage to most major splats, if the Storyteller allows it.]</span></span> <hr />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-03-2016, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T11:11:25-08:00","id":839313,"title":"","content":"2nd post with unfinished notes, for easier editing. Some are near final state, others could really use some feedback. <hr /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Blackout</u><br /> Humanity, and more specifically what triggers large reactions in masses of humanity, are common tools of God-Machine observation. Angels have access to these information streams by virtue of being connected to the God-Machine, and Demons are intimately familiar with the consequences of these reporting mechanisms. By identifying the underlying local mechanisms that support this network, and flooding them with Aether, the Demon can cut of mortal awareness from the Machine\u2019s information assets for a time.</span></span><br /> <b>Example Prerequisites</b>: Interference, Diversion<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Intelligence + Subterfuge + Primum - <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">the highest Wits present + the highest Angel Rank (if any)</span></span><br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 3 Aether<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dramatic Failure</b>: The Demon thinks they\u2019ve blocked out the God-Machine\u2019s observation, but has only served to call out their presence. <i>All</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Compromise rolls caused by human observation in the scene now have a -3 penalty. The Demon gains the Surveilled Condition and automatically loses a point of Cover, and may gain the Blackballed Condition at the end of the scene at Storyteller discretion.<br /> <b>Failure</b>: The action fails and the Machine is still alerted to the Demon\u2019s presence. Roll for Compromise at -3 and gain the Surveilled Condition.<br /> <b>Success</b>: The links of information flowing from mortal awareness to the God-Machine are scrambled. Mortal humans no longer provoke or aggravate Compromise rolls for observing demonic activity (though Angels, and Activated Demon-Blooded do, and God-Machine cultists </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>may</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">) for the rest of the scene. However, this does implicate the Demon\u2019s cover when the mess is cleaned up. Roll for Compromise at -3 and gain the Surveilled Condition at the end of the scene.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: Not only does the Demon scramble the link, they manage to obfuscate their presence enough to hide their involvement. Roll for Compromise at -1 penalty, and do not gain the Surveilled Condition.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Ephemeral Reprogramming</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The God-Machine occasionally re-purposes Ghosts and Spirits to fulfill certain goals. Some Unchained have figured out the protocols and methods used to do this (albeit temporarily in most cases), and can now alter an ephemeral's nature and abilities.<br /> [Allow the Demon to edit an Ephemeral entity\u2019s Ban, Bane, Numina, and/or Manifestations. Angels are immune (Exiles </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>aren\u2019t</i>, but incur an additional -5 penalty?). Roll penalized by Rank? Exceptional Success allows for the change to be made permanent with a Willpower dot.]</span></span><br /> <b>Example Prerequisites</b>: <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Only Word that Matters, Identity Theft</span></span><br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Presence + Occult + Primum vs. Resistance + Rank<br /> <b>Action</b>: Extended and Contested (one roll/turn, Target number = Rank + 1 per Numina altered, 2 per Manifestation altered, 3 per Ban or Bane altered)<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1 Aether per roll<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dramatic Failure</b>: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Demon botches the job and temporarily boosts the ephemeral's power while giving it a pressing desire to punish the Demon. The Storyteller picks a number of new Numina and/or Manifestations equal to the Aether spent for the ephemeral to use against the Demon. The powers and thirst for vengeance typically last only a few scenes.<br /> <b>Failure</b>:<br /> <b>Success</b>: </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success</b>: The Demon can embed their changes deep inside the ephemeral and make them a part of its nature. By spending a <i>dot</i> of Willpower, the alterations are a permanent part of the target being. Alternatively, the Demon can apply a beneficial Condition to the ephemeral for free (such as Swooning, or Leveraged).<br /> [Play around with the roll interval? Maybe let it be variable, with duration of effects lasting for Successes in Interval? Or have an Instant and Contested option for a single change for one Scene effect - such as when you desperately need to alter a Ban, Bane, or Manifestation?]</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Fractured Space</u> (? Is this the name of a video game? Might need a name change?)<br /> The God-Machine often uses spatial folding to hide Its Facilities and expedite the transfer of materials from one location to another. Many Psychopomps still remember bits of how they accomplished these feats. That knowledge has been codified into an Exploit that lets Unchained mold the local spatial topography for a time.<br /> <b>Example Prerequisites</b>: Blink of the Eye, Imagine<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Intelligence + Science + Primum<br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 3 Aether<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dramatic Failure</b>: </span></span>Space warps, trapping the Demon in a self-contained bubble of warped space until they reach 3 successes on an Extended Primum roll, or can teleport out of the bubble.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Failure</b>: The Demon is unable to alter the local spatial mapping.<br /> <b>Success</b>: </span></span>The Demon is able to warp how local space operates, making one of the below changes, or another one approved of by the Storyteller:<br /> * Create a region of space that leads to another region of space (like a portal or wormhole) within Successes * 10 yards [meters?], no more than the Demon's Size + Primum in diameter.<br /> * &quot;Stretch&quot; a region of space an extra Successes * 5 cubic yards, no more than the Demon's Size + Primum in diameter (minimum 1). Treat the amount of area inside the affected region as if it had the additional space as empty air. Note: This can affect the range penalties/modifiers of firearms/weapons passing through the altered space.<br /> * &quot;Compress&quot; a region of space no more that Successes * 5 cubic yards by the Demon's Size + Primum in cubic yards (minimum of 1 cubic yard). Objects that reach the boundary of the affected space need to only travel the altered dimensions before reaching the other side. Note: This can affect the range penalties/modifiers of firearms/weapons passing through the altered space.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success</b>: Space is warped, but the Demon also manages to install a number of &quot;backdoors&quot; allowing them to selective turn of and on the alterations for the duration of the Exploit.</span></span><br /> [Comments: I love multi-use, flexible powers like Newton's Nightmares. This lets a Demon get in on spatial manipulation, making portals, places bigger on the inside than out, &quot;closer than it appears&quot; boobytraps, and redirection or mirror zones.]<br /> [Swap out Successes in the calculations for pure Primum? Play around with the distance multipliers?]<br /> <br /> <u>All In</u><br /> You lean hard on probability, inverting the bell curve so that extreme result become more common than more moderate outcomes. The slightest misstep leads to almost comical failure, and most successful actions have outstanding results.<br /> <b>Example Prerequisites</b>: Victory At Any Price, Failure At Any Cost, Like The Movies, Left or Right<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Presence + Science + Primum vs Resolve + Primum<br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant and Contested<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 3 Aether<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dramatic Failure</b>: </span></span>You manage to foul up your own luck, downgrading Failure to Dramatic Failure, Success to Failure, and Exceptional Success to mere Success<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Failure</b>: Your manipulations are too ambitious and cancel themselves out.<br /> <b>Success</b>: </span></span>Each actor in the Scene that fails to gain more Successes than the Demon suffers from an astounding streak of luck - both good and bad. Any Failures are downgraded to Dramatic Failures if even 1 die turns up a 1, and they get Exceptional Success on 3 Successes instead of 5.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success</b>: You maintain a bit more control over individual probability manipulations, allowing you to determine whether a specific action will be downgraded or upgraded a number of times up to your Primum.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: For when you need things to happen <i>spectacularly</i>. If the Demon can plan ahead and take advantage of Teamwork and Momentum, they can score ES after ES, while they pile on negative modifiers so their foes suffer a congo line of DFs. This can easily turn around though. Regardless, Scenes are bound to be <i>interesting</i>.]</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><u>Demonic Might</u> (aka. Giant's Punch, Clobbering Time)</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Sometimes, a Demon just has to break things, physically and immediately. You can send a surge of Aether through your limbs, strengthening muscles and converting it into kinetic energy.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Example Prerequisites</b>: Knockout Punch, Shatter<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Strength + Brawl or Weaponry + Primum - Defense (optional)<br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1 Aether<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dramatic Failure</b>: </span></span>Your efforts to bolster your physical might backfires. You suffer from the Arm Wrack Tilt and reduce your Strength score by half (round down, minimum of 1) for the remainder of the Scene.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Failure</b>: Power is expended, but you fail to bolster your might.<br /> <b>Success</b>: </span></span>Energy courses through your limbs and enables you to deal devastating blows. You can either increase your effective Strength for carrying or feats of strength by your Primum for the Scene, or make a Brawl or Weaponry attack (using the Exploit's activation pool, minus the target's Defense) that has Armor Piercing and ignores Durability equal to half your Primum (round up).<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success</b>: Power surges through you with exceptional efficiency and effectiveness. You can apply a Tilt such as Knocked Down to a target, permanently reduce an object's Durability or Structure by half your Primum (round up), or if you deal enough damage to destroy an object or fill an opponent's health with Aggravated damage, make an additional attack roll at a nearby target using the a dice pool of the remaining damage.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: A non-Form dependent Strength booster, though the way in which it works doesn't step on Inhuman Strength's toes. The attack action adds armor penetration on top of letting the Demon add their Primum to the attack roll. Exception Success lets you punch <i>through</i> people, which is always nice in a pinch.]</span></span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-10-2016, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T13:25:57-08:00","id":843595,"title":"","content":"Huh. I figured this would have had more activity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T15:27:30-08:00","id":843636,"title":"","content":"Give it time. It'll catch on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T19:44:07-08:00","id":843755,"title":"","content":"<u>Ricochet</u> (Cacophonic)<br /> Everyone knows the scene - two opposing gunmen are facing off from behind the safety of cover until by chance one hits the right surface at the right angle. For a Destroyer, they don\u2019t have to resort to luck for such an occurrence to happen. By pushing momentum, velocity, and trajectory, a demon can hit a target without even being pointed in the right direction though pushing reality to inflict violence goes unseen for only so long. A demon can only use this Embed a number of time per scene equal to half their Primium rounded up.<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Wits + Firearms \u2013 Concealment modifier<br /> <b>Action</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b>: The bullet follows the wrong path and deals the weapon\u2019s rating in lethal damage to the demon.<br /> <b>Failure</b>: The bullet careens harmlessly into the air or a surface.<br /> <b>Success</b>: For each success decrease the concealment modifier to a minimum of 0 before the shot is fired.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: The shot finds a path that seems physically plausible allowing the demon\u2019s tampering to go unseen. This shot doesn\u2019t use up one of the scenes allotted use of this Embed.<br /> <br /> <u>One-inch Punch</u> <br /> In Wing Chun, no distance is too great or too small to deliver a devastating blow. Every Destroyer knows that at some point regardless of how thoroughly planned out all combat will end in fisticuffs so having a way to ensure the upper hand is necessary. By utilizing the potential energy in a simple gesture, a demon is able create a \u201cburst\u201d of kinetic energy on contact with an opponent sending them soaring.<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Dexterity + Brawl \u2013 Defense<br /> <b>Action</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b>: The touch creates a kinetic feedback in the demon\u2019s body dealing lethal damage equal to the demon\u2019s Primium and leaving the demon with Stunned Tilt.<br /> <b>Failure</b>: Nothing happens from the touch.<br /> <b>Success</b>: The opponent is thrown success yards away from the demon. If the victim hits a surface, the resulting force of the collision deals bashing damage equal to the number of successes.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: Beyond just the extra successes the victim also receives the Stunned Tilt if they collide with a surface or the Knocked Down Tilt otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T16:56:07-08:00","id":844211,"title":"","content":"Here's my feedback for Vent0's first post. More coming soon. I am not very good with crunch, so take my advice with a spoon of salt.<br /> <br /> <b>Blink of the Eye (Mundane):</b> This is rather similar to the Plasma Drive Propulsion, but with no Aether or Compromise roll required. Observe:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a reflexive action on his turn, the demon can spend one Aether to activate his Plasma Drive to move at a run and take an action. The demon still subtracts his Defense from attacks made on him this turn, and he still benefits from his Speed as above. </div> </div> </div> I'd make the Embed Instant instead of Reflexive, and decrease the distance covered (not sure how much, a distance of about fifty yards seems like a reasonable limit). Also, the Embed should not bypass obstacles or restraints. I don't think a Compromise roll is necessary, this Embed is not on the same level of risk as Voice Of The Machine.<br /> <br /> <b>Wait For It (Instrumental):</b> This seems like it could be incorporated into the Hesitation Embed as an alternate effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Fate Entanglement: </b>You say it affects objects, but then you say it affects individuals too. I'd make the presence of the two targets in the same vicinity a prerequisite. This seems like the perfect Exploit to make a Gadget that is attached to the neck or ankle to control someone's behavior.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure At Any Cost (Cacophonic):</b> This is way too deadly to the Demon for an Embed. Consider using Ellipses and Wasted Time instead.<br /> <br /> <b>Diagnostic (Instrumental):</b> This seems like a version of Like I Built It that also works on living beings and supernatural phenomena. Judging from the name, I'd limit it to the former, and it should diagnose physical details only (no Virtue, Vice, Breaking Points, Aspirations and so on). Revealing if someone is a supernatural should probably be relegated to powers like the Aura Sight and Mind-Reading Technologies.<br /> <br /> <b>Knowledge Indexing (Instrumental):</b> This one seems OK, but Virtue, Vice and Integrity aren't really talents or knowledge. Embeds that discern those traits would probably be Vocal, like Heart's Desire and Sum Of All Fears.<br /> <br /> <b>Mundana Obscura:</b> What about security footage observed by someone who wasn't there when the Demon used this Exploit? Does supernatural detection trigger a Clash Of Wills as usual?<br /> <br /> <b>Stowaway:</b> The Dramatic Failure effect sounds excessive. The Demon could be stuck to the Fetter without even Embeds, requiring an extended Resistance roll to sever the connection, each roll taking one day. Target number of Success is up to the ST. Using Primum as Rank is too much. The rules for Ephemeral Cover show that most Demons would count as Rank 1 or 2. If the Demon gets an Exceptional Success on the activation, he should be able to use Exploits as normal (i.e. requiring a Compromise roll unless they spend 1 willpower point). Treating the Fetter as an Offspring sounds too big for a side effect, as does triggering the Hunted Condition. Also, you can do something similar to this with the Living Shadow Exploit.<br /> <br /> <b>True Lies (Vocal):</b> Sounds good, but should last for the scene with a Success, and up to a week at most with an Exceptional Success.<br /> <br /> <b>Fuel Leak (Cacophonic):</b> Aetheric Bleed is very tied to the way a Demon regains Aether in their true form, so it's probably not suited for other supernaturals. Also, I think this might work better as an Exploit or Technology.<br /> <br /> <b>Essence Burn: </b>You might wanna use Pendragon's version of the Essence Drain Technology, replicated below.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Demonic Form power \u2018Essence Drain\u2019 can do more than just suck the Essence out of Ephemeral beings. Any time the Demon uses this power to enhance an attack roll it may spend a point of willpower and make a reflexive Aetheric Resonance roll, gathering up to the damage dealt points of Aether. Wounds harvested this way appear to dissolve, leaving bizarre patches of glitchy nothingness where a normal wound should be. This damage is persistent and does not heal without magical intervention. Harming a human this way is cause for a compromise roll.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-08-2016, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T11:44:43-08:00","id":844641,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=844211#post844211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's my feedback for Vent0's first post. More coming soon. I am not very good with crunch, so take my advice with a spoon of salt.<br /> <br /> <b>Blink of the Eye (Mundane):</b> This is rather similar to the Plasma Drive Propulsion, but with no Aether or Compromise roll required. Observe:<br /> I'd make the Embed Instant instead of Reflexive, and decrease the distance covered (not sure how much, a distance of about fifty yards seems like a reasonable limit). Also, the Embed should not bypass obstacles or restraints. I don't think a Compromise roll is necessary, this Embed is not on the same level of risk as Voice Of The Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the purpose of the Embed was for movement enhancing options that aren't dependent upon one's Form Powers. The precedent for using the Uncertainty principle seems a likely candidate for allowing the Demon to shift their own position (barring the observational constraints). Tying movement to speed was because it is using the &quot;justification&quot; that the Demon &quot;could&quot; have just moved there normally, but no one saw. I might add the addendum about not using it to bypass obstacles (though this removes some of the fun that might be had with it). The risk of Compromise was due to if someone catches your &quot;positional cheating&quot; - you can't hide behind &quot;but I move quick/silently&quot; as a justification for what you just did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=844211#post844211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Wait For It (Instrumental):</b> This seems like it could be incorporated into the Hesitation Embed as an alternate effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hesitation only really affect Initiative. I guess a Near Field effect <i>might</i> stretch it enough, but this is for more regular usage, and it targets <i>events</i>, not <i>people</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=844211#post844211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Fate Entanglement: </b>You say it affects objects, but then you say it affects individuals too. I'd make the presence of the two targets in the same vicinity a prerequisite. This seems like the perfect Exploit to make a Gadget that is attached to the neck or ankle to control someone's behavior.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dang it. I meant objects in a more general programming sense. I'll change it to targets. What are your thoughts on the Exception effect? Control of Consequences transferred, or multi-targeting?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=844211#post844211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Failure At Any Cost (Cacophonic):</b> This is way too deadly to the Demon for an Embed. Consider using Ellipses and Wasted Time instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>I basically wanted a mirror of Victory At Any Price, but instead of ensuring a Demon's success, ensuring a target's Failure. The problem is that this can get disproportionately powerful. You could, in theory, make even a Rank 5 Angel/Potency 10 Whatever fail at anything. Great for being a troll, bad for anything near game/power balance. But then there is the question of how to actually limit such an ability?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=844211#post844211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Diagnostic (Instrumental):</b> This seems like a version of Like I Built It that also works on living beings and supernatural phenomena. Judging from the name, I'd limit it to the former, and it should diagnose physical details only (no Virtue, Vice, Breaking Points, Aspirations and so on). Revealing if someone is a supernatural should probably be relegated to powers like the Aura Sight and Mind-Reading Technologies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll probably drop the Supernatural detection. The intent was for simple physical inspection, but Conditions can vary a bit in source. I'll think about adding in some note regarding ST oversight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=844211#post844211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Knowledge Indexing (Instrumental):</b> This one seems OK, but Virtue, Vice and Integrity aren't really talents or knowledge. Embeds that discern those traits would probably be Vocal, like Heart's Desire and Sum Of All Fears.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I'd think one might be aware of what their Virtue/Vice are (though Integrity, agreed, isn't likely). Might drop them anyways - the Embed already has enough it can uncover.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=844211#post844211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mundana Obscura:</b> What about security footage observed by someone who wasn't there when the Demon used this Exploit? Does supernatural detection trigger a Clash Of Wills as usual?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll add in a note regarding Clash of Wills. I'll also clarify that this is an Observation effect - live viewing (even from a camera) falls under the Exploit's influence, but post-hoc viewing (such as from photos or recordings) does not. The intent is infiltration, not explicit invisibility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=844211#post844211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Stowaway:</b> The Dramatic Failure effect sounds excessive. The Demon could be stuck to the Fetter without even Embeds, requiring an extended Resistance roll to sever the connection, each roll taking one day. Target number of Success is up to the ST. Using Primum as Rank is too much. The rules for Ephemeral Cover show that most Demons would count as Rank 1 or 2. If the Demon gets an Exceptional Success on the activation, he should be able to use Exploits as normal (i.e. requiring a Compromise roll unless they spend 1 willpower point). Treating the Fetter as an Offspring sounds too big for a side effect, as does triggering the Hunted Condition. Also, you can do something similar to this with the Living Shadow Exploit.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was modeled on Demon House, but instead of area possession, it mimics Fetter. I'll likely downgrade the Dramatic Failure effect, so one roll doesn't screw you. The purpose of Primum = Rank was merely for Fetter calculations. I need to revise once I have access to the rule books again. I'm going to ditch the Offspring text - too complicated. This is for longer term &quot;haunting&quot;, compared to Living Shadow's movement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=844211#post844211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>True Lies (Vocal):</b> Sounds good, but should last for the scene with a Success, and up to a week at most with an Exceptional Success.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good, will do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=844211#post844211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Fuel Leak (Cacophonic):</b> Aetheric Bleed is very tied to the way a Demon regains Aether in their true form, so it's probably not suited for other supernaturals. Also, I think this might work better as an Exploit or Technology.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was primarily intended as the foundational Embed for Essence Burn, but also as a subtle way to mess with other Supernaturals. I threw out the option of sticking a variant of Aether Bleed on targets merely to conserve space and prevent making more Conditions to keep track of - it slowly drains Fuel Stat over time, which fits the flavor. Other option is the original - Lose extra Fuel Stat each time you normally do. The idea being a cunning Demon can tag a target with this, then get them to waste their juice, before re-engaging from a position of strength.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=844211#post844211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Essence Burn: </b>You might wanna use Pendragon's version of the Essence Drain Technology, replicated below.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Demonic Form power \u2018Essence Drain\u2019 can do more than just suck the Essence out of Ephemeral beings. Any time the Demon uses this power to enhance an attack roll it may spend a point of willpower and make a reflexive Aetheric Resonance roll, gathering up to the damage dealt points of Aether. Wounds harvested this way appear to dissolve, leaving bizarre patches of glitchy nothingness where a normal wound should be. This damage is persistent and does not heal without magical intervention. Harming a human this way is cause for a compromise roll.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the whole idea behind this was a direct interface with Supernaturals (affecting Fuel Stats), as well as copying the mechanics of &quot;Mana Burn&quot; (see Warcarft 3's Demon Hunter ability of the same name for the general feel) - Remove resources and deal damage with said removal. It actually isn't intended to deal any damage otherwise, so Pendragon's modification wouldn't have any effect. <br /> <br /> The cap on it is a Demon's Aether per Turn, keeping it low for the most part. Though Unchained Going Loud can deal <i>devastating</i> amounts of damage with it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T14:36:22-08:00","id":844741,"title":"","content":"I'm squeamish about making my own embeds/exploits, since I haven't gotten familiar enough with what's out there already, you know, not wanting to making something redundant (kind've ironic, now that I think of it). Would they have to emphasize scientific concepts, as a necessity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T19:10:42-08:00","id":844863,"title":"","content":"<u>Fuel Reserves</u> (Instrumental)<br /> Even when the needle hits E and the little orange gas pump illuminates, the average gas tank still contains a few gallons that can mean the difference between getting to a station and not. For a Guardian, relying on man-made machines to assist them in their labors is a constant liability. To make these machines a little more useful, a demon can tamper with this fuel consumption to allow them to run for longer than they should.<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Wits + Science<br /> <b>Action</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b>: Instead of becoming more efficient, the engine seizes up on itself killing its power and dealing damage to its structure equal to the demon\u2019s Primium.<br /> <b>Failure</b>: The machine continues to consume its fuel at its normal rate.<br /> <b>Success</b>: For each success, increase the amount of units of fuel (gas, battery, solar, etc.) available to the machine by one.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: The device becomes a paragon of fuel consumption in the hands of the demon. As long as the demon is the only that operates the machine it will never run out of power.<br /> <br /> <u>Lock Down</u><br /> Security is something that every Guardian cherishes as one of the Unchained. In certain emergency situations it is then necessary then that they be able to prevent entrance and control the movement of individuals in a complex. If the demon has access to at least one key that can be used to lock an entrance to a complex, they can secure all closed portals at once.<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Wits + Larceny<br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b>: The building becomes antagonist towards the demon. The demon receives a -3 to any roll within the structure until they roll another failure.<br /> <b>Failure</b>: Nothing happens to the portals.<br /> <b>Success</b>: All closed portals (doors, windows, vents) become locked in place even if they lack a locking mechanism. Any mundane attempt to open the portals receive a penalty equal to the number of successes.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: Beyond just the extra successes the demon gains awareness of all the portals in the complex and can shut a number of portals equal to their Primium. Any supernatural attempt to bypass a portal triggers a Clash of Wills. <br /> <br /> <u>Shield of Faith</u> <br /> Very few of the superstitious and religious beliefs attached to the supernatural in the world hold true when confronted by the real thing, but many still believe in them. This belief is strong and pervasive in humanity and has shaped cultural customs/symbols. For the Guardian that comes into conflict with the other supernatural denizens of the world these symbols can be a powerful resource. By tapping into the collective belief and presenting an appropriate symbol (e.g. crosses, wolfsbane, salt) the demon can terrify the respective supernatural creature (e.g. vampires, werewolves, ghosts).<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Wits + Religion \u2013 Resolve (roll for each opponent available. Gains +1 for each additional opponent)<br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b>: Instead of terrifying the opponent, the creature becomes enraged to kill the demon giving them a +3 on their next attack roll.<br /> <b>Failure</b>: The symbol falls flat often leaving a monster laughing at the demon.<br /> <b>Success</b>: Every opponent that fails this roll gains the Frightened Condition.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: The demon fuels the symbol with such significant psychic energy that the opponent become incapable of acting in its presence. The monster gains the Insensate Tilt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T20:18:03-08:00","id":844884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=844741#post844741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm squeamish about making my own embeds/exploits, since I haven't gotten familiar enough with what's out there already, you know, not wanting to making something redundant (kind've ironic, now that I think of it). Would they have to emphasize scientific concepts, as a necessity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all. Demon thematically uses Spycraft, and the God-Machine/Angel's &quot;Occult Physics&quot; lets you play around with a number of concepts. While references to Quantum Mechanics and Probability Manipulation abound, there is also abstract Symbolism used, and sometimes just overt power (especially with Exploits - Ultimatum's transformation is hardly sciency, and Raise Dead is more straight forward).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-09-2016, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T20:23:19-08:00","id":844886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=844741#post844741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm squeamish about making my own embeds/exploits, since I haven't gotten familiar enough with what's out there already, you know, not wanting to making something redundant (kind've ironic, now that I think of it). Would they have to emphasize scientific concepts, as a necessity?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a lot of powers that don't use science and instead run off exploiting what people &quot;expect&quot;. Like using movie-physics, or making people think your saying/doing something boring and mundane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T13:58:08-08:00","id":845250,"title":"","content":"Hmm. What about an Embed (or would it need to be an Exploit?) that lets the Demon fake Honorary Rank amongst those beings that track it?<br /> <br /> Or something that lets a Demon detect beings in Twilight (even just their presence/absence)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T15:11:47-08:00","id":845300,"title":"","content":"What about an Exploit that utilizes David Hume's Riddle of Induction, where angels temporarily can't tell the difference between demons and angels without closer inspection?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T16:16:57-08:00","id":845340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=845250#post845250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. What about an Embed (or would it need to be an Exploit?) that lets the Demon fake Honorary Rank amongst those beings that track it?<br /> <br /> Or something that lets a Demon detect beings in Twilight (even just their presence/absence)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think for your first idea you would have to decide when you would be using this to determine if it was an embed or exploit. As an embed I could see situations where you could maybe cash in social merits to resist the status or rank of another supernatural following them. As an exploit I could see it as something that effects legend that allows you to create ranks instead of skills or merits.<br /> <br /> For the second idea I had thought of one for Psychopomp's that would be similar to a Seance or ouiji board where they perform a cultural ritual to be able to ask a ghost questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T08:37:22-08:00","id":845657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=845340#post845340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the second idea I had thought of one for Psychopomp's that would be similar to a Seance or ouiji board where they perform a cultural ritual to be able to ask a ghost questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something like this?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Seance</u> (Vocal)<br /> Many human cultures hold special ceremonies invoking their ancestors or spirits to come and give aid or advice. You know the underlying occult triggers that open up these connections and can momentarily trick such beings into giving some sign of their presence.<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Manipulation + Persuasion [or Occult, if you prefer] vs Resistance + Rank<br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant and Contested</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dramatic Failure</b>: You've accidentally funneled too much power into nearby Ephemerals and opened a direct connection to yourself. You have the Open Condition keyed to all nearby Ephemeral entities for the Scene.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Failure</b>: No Ephemeral elects to make itself known.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Success</b>: Treat nearby entities in Twilight as if they had the Image Manifestation, which they then use for free. Unlike a normal usage of the Manifestation, the signs cause by this Embed are very weak and only last 1 Turn. Observers must make a Reflexive Wits + Composure roll to notice such subtle phenomena, with their dice rolls capped by the number of Successes rolled on this Embed.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success</b>: You are able to establish a much stronger connection to Twilight, and nearby beings are now fully visible for the remainder of the Scene (as per a normal use of the Image Manifestation).</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-11-2016, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T09:50:44-08:00","id":845686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=845657#post845657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Something like this?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Seance</u> (Vocal)<br /> Many human cultures hold special ceremonies invoking their ancestors or spirits to come and give aid or advice. You know the underlying occult triggers that open up these connections and can momentarily trick such beings into giving some sign of their presence.<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Manipulation + Persuasion vs Resistance + Rank<br /> <b>Action</b>: Reflexive and Contested</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dramatic Failure</b>: You've accidentally funneled too much power into nearby Ephemerals and opened a direct connection to yourself. You have the Open Condition keyed to all nearby Ephemeral entities for the Scene.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Failure</b>: No Ephemeral elects to make itself known.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Success</b>: Treat nearby entities in Twilight as if they had the Image Manifestation, which they then use for free. Unlike a normal usage of the Manifestation, the signs cause by this Embed are very weak and only last 1 Turn. Observers must make a Wits + Composure roll to notice such subtle phenomena, with their dice rolls capped by the number of Successes rolled on this Embed.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success</b>: You are able to establish a much stronger connection to Twilight, and nearby beings are now fully visible for the remainder of the Scene (as per a normal use of the Image Manifestation).<br /> [Maybe drop the forced appearance, but allow it to combo with Marco Polo to force them to give a sign?]</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think that is in a really solid direction. Do you think that maybe it would be Mundane instead of Vocal just because Psychopomps traditionally worked with ghosts in their angelic incarnations? Also, perhaps the roll could be Manipulation + Occult, to better play on the demon's understanding of cultural customs and symbols that can draw ghosts? I love the Dramatic Failure and Success conditions (perhaps on a success it also draws ghost to the area?). I think for the Exceptional Success you should keep the mandatory manifestation because making it just combo with Marco Polo makes it seem more like an interlock for some cipher. I would say that maybe instead of being visible, the Exceptional Success makes each ghost cause a more significant phenomena than the normal Success such as blood dripping from walls or foggy breath. Maybe on top of that the demon would gain an awareness of how many ghosts there are and what their ranks are?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T10:30:35-08:00","id":845708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=845686#post845686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I think that is in a really solid direction. Do you think that maybe it would be Mundane instead of Vocal just because Psychopomps traditionally worked with ghosts in their angelic incarnations? Also, perhaps the roll could be Manipulation + Occult, to better play on the demon's understanding of cultural customs and symbols that can draw ghosts? I love the Dramatic Failure and Success conditions (perhaps on a success it also draws ghost to the area?). I think for the Exceptional Success you should keep the mandatory manifestation because making it just combo with Marco Polo makes it seem more like an interlock for some cipher. I would say that maybe instead of being visible, the Exceptional Success makes each ghost cause a more significant phenomena than the normal Success such as blood dripping from walls or foggy breath. Maybe on top of that the demon would gain an awareness of how many ghosts there are and what their ranks are?</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason behind Vocal was, to me, that it seems more communication related (causing the ghost or spirit to appear or give a sign), as opposed to disguise or normality related. I picked Persuasion due to you trying to &quot;sweet talk&quot; the ephemeral into appearing. Occult could very easily be used as well. It was kind of a coin toss for me. I think combos aren't just reserved for Interlocks - this seems like a case where a follow up use of Marco Polo would work to get the beings to give themselves away. But you might be able to do that with MP <i>anyways</i>. &lt;shrug&gt;.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind, this as written isn't limited to ghosts - it can work on Spirits too, at least. Storyteller might need to determine whether it could work on Angels as well. It exploits something inherent to the ephemeral condition, but I can also see Angels having a failsafe immunity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T11:12:00-08:00","id":845734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=845708#post845708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bear in mind, this as written isn't limited to ghosts - it can work on Spirits too, at least. Storyteller might need to determine whether it could work on Angels as well. It exploits something inherent to the ephemeral condition, but I can also see Angels having a failsafe immunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is a solid way to take it by having it effect everyone, but angels which can be spun any way a Storyteller desires. It also fills a badly needed space for demons and their interaction with ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T11:58:12-08:00","id":845755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=845734#post845734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that is a solid way to take it by having it effect everyone, but angels which can be spun any way a Storyteller desires. It also fills a badly needed space for demons and their interaction with ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, though in keeping with Demon's general weakness/non-interaction with the ephemeral, the Embed is design to &quot;suck&quot; (IE, not be very effective vs Twilight entities, at least in regards to other Splats that can easily surpass them in this arena). Invisible Angels lurking nearby in Twilight is still a big risk. Just now you might be able to tell when they are in the room with you.<br /> <hr /><br /> Anyone have any Embed ideas that would be ideal for making into Software Gadgets? Not all Embeds are applicable, and it might be nice to have a broad library of tools you can use off your Stockpiled smart phone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-11-2016, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T12:39:18-08:00","id":845783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=845755#post845755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed, though in keeping with Demon's general weakness/non-interaction with the ephemeral, the Embed is design to &quot;suck&quot; (IE, not be very effective vs Twilight entities, at least in regards to other Splats that can easily surpass them in this arena). Invisible Angels lurking nearby in Twilight is still a big risk. Just now you might be able to tell when they are in the room with you.<br /> <hr /><br /> Anyone have any Embed ideas that would be ideal for making into Software Gadgets? Not all Embeds are applicable, and it might be nice to have a broad library of tools you can use off your Stockpiled smart phone.</div> </div> </div> </div>It definitely succeeds at evoking that feel. It does seem kind of funny that Demon's are supposed to just generally be weak to the ephemeral as a whole and not just angels. That all being said, this Embed is making me think of an Exploit that could possibly allow for some greater interaction with ephemera. Maybe something called &quot;Reap&quot; that allows for the removal of ephemera for the benefit of the Demon? <br /> <br /> About your second point, are you looking for already existing Embeds that can be used as software, or are you looking for the creation of Embeds that lend themselves to the creation of Software Gadgets?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T12:56:25-08:00","id":845793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=845783#post845783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It definitely succeeds at evoking that feel. It does seem kind of funny that Demon's are supposed to just generally be weak to the ephemeral as a whole and not just angels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I've tried to add a few here and there (such as Ephemeral Reprogramming or Essence Burn), but don't want to go overboard. Werewolves are better for tangling with Spirits, Sin-Eaters for Ghosts (and Mages can fill in any holes). Angels <i>would</i> be up the Demon's alley, but the nature of their powers raises certain questions if they have too many that are good vs Angels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=845783#post845783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That all being said, this Embed is making me think of an Exploit that could possibly allow for some greater interaction with ephemera. Maybe something called &quot;Reap&quot; that allows for the removal of ephemera for the benefit of the Demon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Ephemeral Cover?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=845783#post845783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About your second point, are you looking for already existing Embeds that can be used as software, or are you looking for the creation of Embeds that lend themselves to the creation of Software Gadgets?</div> </div> </div> </div>Either? Both? Probably makes sense to start with a list of what is there. I just remember reading through and thinking &quot;this can't be made into software, this can't either, this <i>might</i> be, but how, etc.&quot;.<br /> <br /> I have the plans for an Agency whose schtick is maintaining a library of Software Gadgets, that they sell out the usage of to elite hackers than might be useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T13:38:35-08:00","id":845811,"title":"","content":"Agreed. Your work on those Embeds definitely made the most sense as far as logical steps in closing the gap while not overreaching. <br /> <br /> Ephemeral Cover, does exist and what I described wasn't too far from that. It still feels like there is a hole in Exploits for something else to assist in ephemeral interaction considering how many other tools are at their disposal for everyone else. <br /> <br /> Great idea for an agency. I felt the same way when I read over software gadgets. One thing that I think might help will be in understanding their framework a little better. It seems that they can roughly be broken down into two different groups based on effects and desired use: 1) App like programs that can exist on a computer or other device that doesn't need to be installed into a system to create an effect. Like an app on the phone that allows you to send a form of Anarchism through texts. 2) Software/code that must be installed into a system to use the benefit. Something like a code form of Download Knowledge that can be used on a mainframe that instantly gets to the knowledge desired. I'm not sure if that helps but it is making reading through the list of embeds more clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T14:45:02-08:00","id":845835,"title":"","content":"Embeds that are applied as Software Gadgets:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Cacophonic</b></u><ul><li><u>Apple of Dischord</u>. Ensnares those who read something &quot;infected&quot; with it. Best used as a trap.</li> <li><u>Anarchism</u>. Affects those who read the &quot;enhanced&quot; media. Best used as a trap.</li> <li><u>Breakdown</u>. Messes up those who read affected media. <i>Great</i> for seeding it into system logs and making the sysadmin use Medicine or Occult when trying to diagnose the problem with the network.</li> <li><u>Cause and Effect</u>. ??? This definitely seems like it should work, though I'm not certain how exactly.</li> <li><u>Combustion</u>. It probably <i>could</i> be Installed, though I doubt many would <i>want</i> to.</li> <li><u>Deafen</u>. Trap maybe?</li> <li><u>Devil's Advocate</u>. AKA Feeding the Trolls Poison.</li> <li><u>Fire Drill</u>. Instant distraction?</li> <li><u>Left Or Right</u>.</li> <li><u>Lucky Break</u>.</li> <li><u>On the Mend</u>.</li> <li><u>Password Entropy</u>.</li> <li><u>Sabotage</u>.</li> <li><u>Shifty Eyes</u>.</li> <li><u>Special Someone</u>.</li> <li><u>Victory At Any Price</u>.</li> </ul><br /> <u><b>Instrumental</b></u><ul><li><u>Check Backdrop</u>.</li> <li><u>Data Retrieval</u>.</li> <li><u>Data Wipe</u>.</li> <li><u>Download Knowledge</u>.</li> <li><u>Efficiency</u>.</li> <li><u>Ellipsis</u>.</li> <li><u>Freeze Assets</u>.</li> <li><u>Functional Identity</u>?</li> <li><u>Fungible Knowledge</u>.</li> <li><u>High Of Birth</u>.</li> <li><u>Like I Built It</u>.</li> <li><u>The Map Is Not The Territory</u>.</li> <li><u>Miles Away</u>. Personal Easy Listening.</li> <li><u>Momentum</u>.</li> <li><u>Open Sesame</u>?</li> <li><u>Read Hostility</u>?</li> <li><u>Shift Consequences</u>?</li> <li><u>Synthesis</u>.</li> <li><u>Tag And Release</u>.</li> <li><u>Tools Into Toys</u>.</li> <li><u>Trivia</u>.</li> <li><u>Wasted Time</u>.</li> </ul><br /> <u><b>Mundane</b></u><ul><li><u>Authorized</u>.</li> <li><u>Cuckoo's Egg</u>?</li> <li><u>Don't I Know You</u>.</li> <li><u>Earworm</u>?</li> <li><u>Homogenous Memory</u>.</li> <li><u>Identity Theft</u>.</li> <li><u>Last Place You Look</u>.</li> <li><u>Like The Movies</u>?</li> <li><u>Lost In The Crowd</u>.</li> <li><u>Meaningless</u>.</li> <li><u>Mistaken Identity</u>.</li> <li><u>Never Here</u>.</li> <li><u>Unperson</u>.</li> <li><u>You Can Tell Me</u>.</li> </ul><br /> <u><b>Vocal</b></u><ul><li><u>Animal Communication</u>.</li> <li><u>Borrowed Expertise</u>.</li> <li><u>Common Misconception</u>.</li> <li><u>Everybody Knows</u>. Yay, Viral memes.</li> <li><u>Find The Leak</u>.</li> <li><u>Freudian Slip</u>.</li> <li><u>Heart's Desire</u>.</li> <li><u>Imagine</u>.</li> <li><u>The Look</u>? Mesmerizing video, maybe?</li> <li><u>Loose Lips</u>.</li> <li><u>Mercury Retrograde</u>.</li> <li><u>Muse</u>.</li> <li><u>The Only Word That Matters</u>.</li> <li><u>Remote Link-Up</u>?</li> <li><u>Rhetoric</u>.</li> <li><u>Social Dynamics</u>.</li> <li><u>Social Engineering</u>.</li> <li><u>Strength Through Adversity</u>.</li> <li><u>Sum Of All Fears</u>.</li> <li><u>Tower Of Babel</u>.</li> <li><u>Trust No One</u>.</li> <li><u>Voice Of The Machine</u>.</li> <li><u>Vox</u>? Or is this redundant with decent audio software?</li> </ul>So, after listing them all out, was wrong about there not being many Software Gadget options. Also, never piss off Demons that can target your through a chat room or social media, and that Unchained make for great marketing campaign consultants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-14-2016, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T17:00:38-08:00","id":845880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cause and Effect. ??? This definitely seems like it should work, though I'm not certain how exactly.</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe a chat app that allows you to use Wits + Computers to accomplish a predetermined type of roll by sending a randomly-generated message to just the right sort of person to set off the correct chain of events?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T18:35:37-08:00","id":845908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=845880#post845880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Maybe a chat app that allows you to use Wits + Computers to accomplish a predetermined type of roll by sending a randomly-generated message to just the right sort of person to set off the correct chain of events?</div> </div> </div> </div>That has a lot of potential behind it. I eagerly await what comes out from this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T20:06:43-08:00","id":845925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=845880#post845880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Maybe a chat app that allows you to use Wits + Computers to accomplish a predetermined type of roll by sending a randomly-generated message to just the right sort of person to set off the correct chain of events?</div> </div> </div> </div>Stochastic terrorism was the first thing that came to my mind, but that might be a better one for Strength Through Adversity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T08:57:52-07:00","id":847105,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Fax</u> (Instrumental)<br /> The Demon uses a precise message or pattern to symbolically link two documents together, ensuring that they match perfectly - currently, and copying any changes in the future, as well. Unchained have often used this as a secure form of communication, as well as a method of making Pacts at a distance.<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Wits + Academics<br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dramatic Failure</b>: The linking between the two documents becomes &quot;leaky&quot;, copying their text to a randomly chosen other media near one of the two bound documents. This will most assuredly cause complications for the Demon in the future.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Failure</b>: Some mistake in the wording or occult manipulations fouls up the binding, ensuring the two documents remain two distinct documents.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Success</b>: The Demon manages to use a specific phrase or message to bind a document to another one featuring the same text or pattern. Alterations to the text on one of them simultaneously appear upon the other, ensuring they remain in sync. The linking last up to Successes in weeks, or until cancelled (such as by ripping up one of the documents), whichever comes first.</span></span><br /> <br /> Note that the paired document doesn't have to actually exist at the moment the Embed is used - the first physical document that replicates the same message or pattern will be the one the original is linked to. This allows for Demons to pre-arrange a system by which they copy pass-phrases, entangle them, then write out their communications. In the modern age, it also allows them to fax or email such missives. This still must occur within the Embed's normal duration, and counts against the remaining time.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success</b>: The binding is more lasting than normal, and is able to exist indefinitely, as long as the two linked documents do.<br /> <br /> [<u>Comments</u>: This now lets Demons get in on secret messages and automatic writing. Using a pre-arranged sequence of phrases, one of them can write up and bind a paper, with the other copying the phrase upon another afterward. Then they can communicate using this archaic, but very secure, &quot;chat room&quot;. At least, until one of them loses their file...<br /> <br /> The Pact ability coupled with the Indefinite duration on exception success also lets an imprisoned Demon craft a message/Pact, then wait for someone to accidentally copy their key-phrase, allowing for mysterious messages, and deals struck from afar.]</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-14-2016, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T08:30:03-07:00","id":848193,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Would an Exploit that <i>removes</i> Conditions/Tilts be appropriate? Affliction (and other abilities) can add them, but what about &quot;curing&quot; them? Name it Miracle or Eraser? Obviously it shouldn't be able to remove Conditions like Burned or Hunted. Or does this functionality already exist in the form of Pacts, and should remain there? Though a general purpose Remove Condition power would also be able to strip beneficial Conditions too. Or maybe it just lets you swap one Condition for another? Rename to Corruption, then?<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T11:30:56-07:00","id":848293,"title":"","content":"I could see this being something that an Analyst could do when they Go Loud by combining Affliction and some other Exploit. Maybe Newton's Nightmares so that you could have a variety of affects that could blanket over an entire area? Break to Heal or Eye for an Eye?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T07:31:04-07:00","id":848779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=848293#post848293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see this being something that an Analyst could do when they Go Loud by combining Affliction and some other Exploit. Maybe Newton's Nightmares so that you could have a variety of affects that could blanket over an entire area? Break to Heal or Eye for an Eye?</div> </div> </div> </div>So restrict it to Lambdas and Analysts Going Loud?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T07:42:15-07:00","id":848784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=848779#post848779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So restrict it to Lambdas and Analysts Going Loud?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah if you feel like that still allows you to do what you want. I just think creating a straight Exploit that could do that would be stepping over other Exploits and mechanics. I was thinking of a Lambda Gadget with Affliction and Eye for an Eye that takes the shape of a syringe maybe that allows you to remove a condition from one person and then inflict it on another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T07:36:05-07:00","id":849249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=848784#post848784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah if you feel like that still allows you to do what you want. I just think creating a straight Exploit that could do that would be stepping over other Exploits and mechanics. I was thinking of a Lambda Gadget with Affliction and Eye for an Eye that takes the shape of a syringe maybe that allows you to remove a condition from one person and then inflict it on another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe? To me it just seems like &quot;Affliction, but the opposite&quot;, which doesn't feel like it should require combining with another power just to get it to work. I'll think on it a bit more. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Finders, Keepers</u> (Cacophonic)<br /> Matter and energy cannot be created or destroyed (baring edge cases). So too with the more abstract resources, as Demons collecting Aether from Angelic Essence know. You can scavenge the energies others spend or lose to replenish your own. When activating this Embed, the Demon chooses some expendable resources they possess (such as Willpower or Aether) and tries to draw in like energies.<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Dexterity + Larceny<br /> <b>Action</b>: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dramatic Failure</b>: You've fumbled your scavenging attempt and end up losing whatever your were trying to take, be it Willpower, Aether, or some other resource.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Failure</b>: Whatever you were trying to recover slips through your metaphorical fingers.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Success</b>: Whenever someone else expends or loses the resource declared when activating the Embed this turn, you gain it in a 2-to-1 ratio. You can only recover a number of points in this way up to your Successes. For example, if you are trying to collect Willpower, and 3 Willpower points are spent this turn, you gain 1 point of Willpower. If 4 had been spent, you would have gained 2, unless you only rolled a single Success - in which case, you'd still only gain 1 Willpower point.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success</b>: You are able to cast your net far and wide, letting little escape your pull. You instead can harvest any expended resources instead of declaring a type (though not all may be useful or convertible, as determined by the Storyteller). Total points collected between types are still limited by the total successes rolled.<br /> <b>Notes</b>: It is up to the Storyteller how broad the resources harvested can be. Health is probably not a good idea, but it is possible some of the other Supernatural power sources might be converted into Aether for the Demon, perhaps at a reduced rate of 3-to-1 or more. Angelic Essence is probably best left to normal Aether collection mechanisms.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Maybe this should be targeted and penalized, but last the Scene? Modify the efficiency? This makes a great spring-board to various other &quot;leeching&quot; effects, for the inclusion into Gadgets, Interlocks, Lambdas and such. I deliberately left the &quot;resources&quot; collected open ended, in case someone is using non-standard ones in their game, like Fatigue, Strain, etc., or if this is incorporated into a Gadget given to another being.]</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-12-2016, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T07:49:02-07:00","id":849257,"title":"","content":"Whoa. Finders, Keepers looks interesting. Just some polishing in presentation, and it's good to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T08:10:39-07:00","id":849275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=849257#post849257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whoa. Finders, Keepers looks interesting. Just some polishing in presentation, and it's good to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made some edits. What else needs to be changed? Any thought on switching it to a targeted, Scene long ability?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T08:20:09-07:00","id":849278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=849275#post849275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I made some edits. What else needs to be changed? Any thought on switching it to a targeted, Scene long ability?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I think the current version works well. Though this is my personal opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T08:24:55-07:00","id":849282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=849249#post849249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe? To me it just seems like &amp;quot;Affliction, but the opposite&amp;quot;, which doesn't feel like it should require combining with another power just to get it to work. I'll think on it a bit more.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about something called &quot;Unction&quot; that plays on the use of oil in the healing services of numerous religions? Perhaps that practice developed out of some innate knowledge about the God Machine and it's use of oil. For demons, they can use oil in any form to remove conditions because it allows the person to &quot;run&quot; smoother. Maybe on an exceptional success they could even remove supernatural templates temporarily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T08:03:21-07:00","id":855075,"title":"","content":"Inspired by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a>'s post <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=830669#post830669\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Face Off</b></u> (Mundane)<br /> Sometimes Demons need to change their appearance without changing their actual Cover. When unobserved, they can make alterations to their physical form (but not their clothes - for that, see Quick Change). Note that these cannot be drastic changes - no restored or missing limbs, etc., it is limited to only those that could be accomplished with mundane disguise, given sufficient skill, time, and supplies (but handled instantaneously via the Embed). For more thorough deception, Cover alterations or Exploits are warranted.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dice Roll</b>: Manipulation + Subterfuge<br /> <b>Action</b>: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dramatic Failure</b>: Your efforts at disguise fail utterly, giving you distinguishing and obvious markings (or making you look like a clown).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Failure</b>: You fail to significantly alter your appearance. Maybe some feature is off, but barely anything noticeable.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Success</b>: You can alter a number of your physical features, masking your real weight, facial features, ethnicity, etc. These changes last for the remainder of the Scene.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success</b>: Your facility with disguise exceeds mere change, letting you impersonate someone whose appearance you know (within the Embeds constraints, of course - if your current Cover is missing a leg, this won't give you a working one even if the person you are impersonating has two).<br /> <b>Notes</b>: This doesn't produce supporting documents (see Authorized to fake that), affect clothing (see Quick Change), or alter your voice (see Vox).</span></span><br /> <br /> <u><b>Form of the Beast</b></u><br /> Tales abound of Demons turning people or themselves into animals. With this Exploit, those stories have merit. You can alter the facet of a target's (including yourself) identity, specifically that relating to what species they are.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Example Prerequisites</b>: Face Off, Animal Communication, Deep Cover<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Intelligence + Animal Ken + Primum - Stamina + Resolve<br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1 Aether + 1 per change in Size<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dramatic Failure</b>: You alterations backfire, causing either an unintended target to transform into what you wanted, or for the target to transform into something you didn't intend (such as instead of turning a charging Stigmatic into a frog, you change them into a rhino).</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: You try to alter their species and come up with nothing, though the target gets a general sense that you tried to change their shape.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The target transforms into the desired animal for the rest of the Scene, or until you voluntarily end the Exploit. Use the animal's Size, Speed, and other inherent traits (such as flight for most birds)</span></span></span></span></span></span>, but keep the target's Attributes (though the Storyteller may rule that they are expressed differently - you might be a strong squirrel, but you are still a squirrel). You may spend 1 Aether to maintain the change for additional scenes without reactivating the Exploit.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success</b>: Your control over physical identity extends beyond shape. You can now also choose to use the animal's attributes instead of the target's (giving yourself great gorilla Strength, or the target the Intelligence of a gerbil). If mental and social scores are reduced to animal level, the target looses the ability to understand speech or act on anything other than their instincts the turn after the change occurs. You can spend 1 additional Aether each scene to maintain this effect in addition to the previous Aether spent.<br /> <b>Note</b>: If you transform yourself or another Demon into an animal, they must still act in Cover for that animal or risk Compromise. Beings with multiple forms, such as Unchained with their Covers, or the many forms a Werewolf can take render offensive use less effective - a Demon can switch to an unaffected Cover or their Demonic Form, a Werewolf can change to a different shape, or a Mage can use their magic to transform themselves into another form (or &quot;back&quot; to their old one).</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-20-2018, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:32:23-07:00","id":856012,"title":"","content":"Yes, I need to fill in all those placeholders I've left lying around.<br /> <br /> But for something (else) new! What does anyone think about &quot;Meta-Embeds&quot;? Like Meta-Magic in D&amp;D 3/3.5, these serve solely to modify other Embeds (and Exploits). Kinda like how Incepts modify Numina. These would let you use Embeds in new ways, like target people based on userID/Forum handle, or have an Embed trigger upon a condition. Or would this best be handled by Lambdas and Interlocks? Merits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T14:39:47-07:00","id":857929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=855075#post855075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Placeholders for powers inspired by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a>'s post <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=830669#post830669\">here</a>]<br /> <br /> <u><b>Face Off</b></u> (Mundane)<br /> [Desc] [Change your physical appearance, but not clothes, as that is covered by Quick Change]<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dice Roll</b>: Manipulation + Subterfuge<br /> <b>Action</b>: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dramatic Failure</b>: </span></span>[Get distinguishing features]<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Failure</b>: [No Effect]</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Success</b>: [Change features and characteristics, giving Disguise bonuses based on successes]</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success</b>: [Can now perfectly imitate someone]<br /> <b>Notes</b>: [Can't change Size, or affect physical Tilts, such as a missing leg causing Leg Wrack]</span></span><br /> <br /> <u><b>Form of the Beast</b></u><br /> [Desc] [Transforms target into an animal. Helpless or demeaning animals for foes, helpful animals for allies or the Demon themselves]<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Example Prerequisites</b>: Face Off, Animal Communication, Deep Cover<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Intelligence + Animal Ken + Primum - Stamina + Resolve<br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1 Aether [?]<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dramatic Failure</b>: [Backfires a harmful transformation, or twists a helpful transformation into something useless]</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: [Nope]</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: [Target changes into selected animal until the Demon ends the Exploit. Last for Successes in Scenes/Days? Variable costs?]</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success</b>: [Allow for changing to toggle back and forth? Permanent Change?]</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> Hey, sorry for the delay. <br /> <br /> I don't think Face-Off should have arbitrary drawbacks. I'm saying this mostly to contain my urge of limiting powers. Since this Embed is similar to Quick Change, I believe the Demon should be relatively alone and unobserved to use it. One Success is enough to make it last for a scene, but it doesn't change anything other than the appearance. In other words, you don't conjure new documents or alter the memories of observers (but you can use other Embeds and Exploits to do that). An Exceptional Success might give a +2 to Subterfuge rolls and/or Spoofing, but it wouldn't extend the duration. I imagine this Embed would be used to get out of trouble quickly and slipping into places without having your true face caught by surveillance. Extended infiltration would require more legwork, such as a new Cover, Legend, Allies Into Gold, Forced Relationship and so on.<br /> <br /> Form Of The Beast, being an Exploit, can break the &quot;must be alone and unobserved&quot; rule that Demons usually follow when changing their shapes. You could add one scene to the duration with 1 Aether without needing to re-roll. If you spent a willpower point on the activation roll to cancel the Compromise, you don't have to spend more, but changing into an animal that is grossly inaccurate for the area requires a Compromise of its own. You can toggle between your Covers and your chosen animal, but with an Exceptional Success, you may also toggle between different animals. You may assume partial or complete Demonic Form while being an animal, following the usual rules (if you can use Context Matters to explain your robot animal form, you get the usual benefits of that Exploit).<br /> <br /> Excellent work. How about an Exploit that allows shape-shifting on the molecular level? Instead of turning the Demon into a different person or an animal, it turns him into an object of roughly similar Size. He can become a complex machine with a minimal Size of 1, and the spent Aether allows him to work as if possessing a full battery. The maximum Size is [Primum + additional Aether spent]. He may distribute his Primum among additional Durability and/or Equipment Bonus. He may use Embeds on himself, on others and his immediate surroundings, but not Exploits. This lasts for a scene.<br /> <br /> On an Exceptional Success, the Demon may manifest up to [Primum] Demonic Form advantages as he wants with no additional Aether cost for the rest of the scene, effectively turning himself into a temporary Multi-Demonic Form Gadget. For safer and less Aether-costly items, he should build Gadgets as usual.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T18:38:40-07:00","id":858661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=857929#post857929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hey, sorry for the delay. <br /> <br /> I don't think Face-Off should have arbitrary drawbacks. I'm saying this mostly to contain my urge of limiting powers. Since this Embed is similar to Quick Change, I believe the Demon should be relatively alone and unobserved to use it. One Success is enough to make it last for a scene, but it doesn't change anything other than the appearance. In other words, you don't conjure new documents or alter the memories of observers (but you can use other Embeds and Exploits to do that). An Exceptional Success might give a +2 to Subterfuge rolls and/or Spoofing, but it wouldn't extend the duration. I imagine this Embed would be used to get out of trouble quickly and slipping into places without having your true face caught by surveillance. Extended infiltration would require more legwork, such as a new Cover, Legend, Allies Into Gold, Forced Relationship and so on.<br /> <br /> Form Of The Beast, being an Exploit, can break the &quot;must be alone and unobserved&quot; rule that Demons usually follow when changing their shapes. You could add one scene to the duration with 1 Aether without needing to re-roll. If you spent a willpower point on the activation roll to cancel the Compromise, you don't have to spend more, but changing into an animal that is grossly inaccurate for the area requires a Compromise of its own. You can toggle between your Covers and your chosen animal, but with an Exceptional Success, you may also toggle between different animals. You may assume partial or complete Demonic Form while being an animal, following the usual rules (if you can use Context Matters to explain your robot animal form, you get the usual benefits of that Exploit).<br /> <br /> Excellent work. How about an Exploit that allows shape-shifting on the molecular level? Instead of turning the Demon into a different person or an animal, it turns him into an object of roughly similar Size. He can become a complex machine with a minimal Size of 1, and the spent Aether allows him to work as if possessing a full battery. The maximum Size is [Primum + additional Aether spent]. He may distribute his Primum among additional Durability and/or Equipment Bonus. He may use Embeds on himself, on others and his immediate surroundings, but not Exploits. This lasts for a scene.<br /> <br /> On an Exceptional Success, the Demon may manifest up to [Primum] Demonic Form advantages as he wants with no additional Aether cost for the rest of the scene, effectively turning himself into a temporary Multi-Demonic Form Gadget. For safer and less Aether-costly items, he should build Gadgets as usual.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll incorporate those details once I'm not on my phone. <br /> <br /> Do you think the item idea might be handled by a Cover modification? Maybe a merit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-03-2016, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T09:49:24-07:00","id":865554,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a> updated the prior 2 powers.<br /> <br /> And now a new one inspired by <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/864954-primordial-sorcery-homebrew?p=865458#post865458\">here</a>. <hr /><br /> <u><b>Forge the Legend</b></u><br /> [Desc] [Takes the stories told about legendary items and makes them &quot;real&quot; the same way Urban Legend does with its characters, but in reverse.]<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Example Prerequisites</b>: Everybody Knows,<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Intelligence + Crafts + Primum - [2 * Relic's Dot rating?]<br /> <b>Action</b>: Extended?<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1 Aether per dot<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dramatic Failure</b>: [Cursed Item]</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: [Dismal Failure and spent resources]</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: [Creates/&quot;Enchants&quot; item of legend as a Relic, using those rules to replicate the storied abilities. Powers provided by flimsy Cover-like effect - investigation reveals it as a fake and ends the effect]</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success</b>: [More resilient? Takes less time? Ex!Success Condition?]<br /> <b>Note</b>: </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>[Needs to leverage an existing storied item, and only replicates the storied powers to the best of the Relic rules. <i>Can</i> use Urban Legend to start the story, then this once it hit Critical Mass.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T07:30:05-07:00","id":882851,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><u><b>Miracle</b></u> [Alt name? Eraser?]<br /> Demons are naturally adept at manipulating relational features of other beings, trading relationships and addictions like currency via Pacts. But sometimes, a Demon needs to get rid of something in a more immediate manner than Pacting will allow, or from subjects who are unwilling to part with such traits. By means of this Exploit, a Demon declares some personal Condition or Tilt the target possesses, removing it from them to fizzle into nothingness. This might be beneficial, such as calming someone's fear (removing the Shaken or Frightened Condition), &quot;healing&quot; the limbs (removing Arm Wrack or Leg Wrack Tilts), or detrimental, such as clouding their clarity of though (removing the Informed Condition).<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Example Prerequisites</b>: Anarchism, Breakdown, On The Mend<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Intelligence + Medicine + Primum<br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 2 Aether<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dramatic Failure</b>: Rather than remove the desired effect, the Demon <i>gives</i> the target a undesirable (to the Demon) Condition or Tilt.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Aether fizzles into nothing as the Demon is unable to break the connection between effect and target.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Demon uncouples the connection between the designated personal Condition or Tilt and its subject. Such effects are removed without actually being Resolved (meaning they don't grant a Beat). If the Condition or Tilt was representing some defect or damage (such as a missing limb), that flaw is also removed. Nothing prevents such Conditions or Tilts from being re-applied, however. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success</b>: The Demon removes the effect with a flood of power, replacing it with a minor Condition or Tilt of their own (such as Inspired or Shaken).</span></span></span></span><br /> <b>Possible Modifiers</b>: <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Condition or Tilt is Persistent (-4). Target has suffered from the Condition or Tilt within the past day (-1 per occasion/Scene). Demon was the one to inflict the Condition or Tilt (+5). Other Conditions dependent upon one to be removed (-3 per dependent Condition).<br /> <b>Note</b>: </span></span></span></span>This can only remove Conditions that are limited to and inherent to the target - Shaken or Swooning are valid, but Leveraged is not because it comes from an external source (No magicking away your Hunted status). The Demon also needs to know (or at least suspect) that the target is under the influence of said Condition/Tilt before using the power. The Storyteller is the final arbiter on what Conditions or Tilts might be able to be removed by this Exploit.</span> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><u><b>Banish</b></u> (AKA Parting the Red Sea)<br /> Humanity thinks it has a good grasp of physics, cause leads to effect, and things being the sum of their components. For the most part, that's right. But as former servants of the God-Machine, Demon understand that you can also change things by altering the relationship between them, and even the identifiers that describe them. Using this Exploit, a Demon can &quot;delete and block&quot; a detail from the scene from having its natural effect, such as removing the flame from a raging inferno or eliminating the effect a mass of water would have on those in the same area.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Example Prerequisites</b>:<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Intelligence + Science + Primum<br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 2 Aether<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dramatic Failure</b>: Rather than removing the Tilt, they strengthen it or cause another one. Additionally, the Demon cannot use this Exploit again in the same scene.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Aether floods into the area... and does n</span></span></span></span>othing.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The targeted Tilt gets removed from the scene and, if it would logically still be applicable, is prevented from reapplying for Successes Turns (or until the Demon cancels the Exploit).</span></span> This means Infernos disappear and won't reignite, even if the surroundings </span>are still aflame. Odd cases such as removing the Flooded Tilt from a body of water might mean the waters part physically, or that the water strangely is only as restrictive as air.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success</b>: The Demon can either extend the duration by a number of turns equal to their Primum, selectively choose who would be affected by the Tilt instead of removing it completely, or replace it for its duration with some other Storyteller approved Tilt.</span></span></span></span><br /> <b>Possible Modifiers</b>: Extreme environment (- the Tilt's level)<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">. Persistent non-supernatural source of the Tilt (-4).<br /> <b>Note</b>: </span></span></span></span>If the Tilt was imposed by a supernatural effect, such as a Mage's spell, or a Beast's Lair Traits, they can contest the Exploit with a Clash of Will. Additional attempts to re-apply such Tilts also are subject to a Clash of Will, with success allowing the Tilt to be applied.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-12-2016, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T07:27:25-07:00","id":883747,"title":"","content":"DELETED MESSAGE","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","user":"lladas","date":". 05-06-2016, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T09:34:12-07:00","id":883850,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>: I like Finders Keepers, Seance and Fax. I believe Forge The Legend could done through a Gadget containing Show Of Power or Urban Legend.<br /> <br /> Miracle sounds iffy. That kind of power seems pretty well covered by Pacts, and its part of the fun to roleplay your Demon buying an debilitating illness or inconvenient relationship to increase their Cover. It's one of the ways they get a better understanding of what mortals go through, even if it's not in a compassionate manner.<br /> <br /> Banish sounds like it should be temporary, even with an Exceptional Success. The Demon could specify that a group of people are protected (no need to limit the group's size by Primum, just use ST fiat), while others can be affected by the Tilt in a surprise tactic, like how Moses parted the Red Sea and then closed it to drown the Egyptians once the Israelites had crossed. We already have Exploits with names like Sermon, Affliction and Rain Of Blood, so why not go ahead and call this one Parting The Red Sea?<br /> <br /> I like your maneuvers for Phoenix Pattern, except the last one. I know you tried to live up to the Style's name, but Going Loud and keeping even a partial Cover sounds like having your cake and eating it. It also takes away the incentive for Demons to build burner Covers in case they need to Go Loud, thus opening another way to investigate them. It occurred to me that a Style that improves Going Loud and one for optimizing the regular Demonic Form should be separate. They are quite distinct conceptually: the first is about sheer power, but the other is more about minimizing the risks of Aetheric Resonance/Compromise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-06-2016, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T09:57:28-07:00","id":883866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=883850#post883850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>: I like Finders Keepers, Seance and Fax. I believe Forge The Legend could done through a Gadget containing Show Of Power or Urban Legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably. I just thought to codify something about making faux &quot;Relics&quot;. Easy copy for something from folklore, but inherently fragile due to the fact it is a knockoff. A Gadget is inherently more stable. &lt;shrug&gt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=883850#post883850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Miracle sounds iffy. That kind of power seems pretty well covered by Pacts, and its part of the fun to roleplay your Demon buying an debilitating illness or inconvenient relationship to increase their Cover. It's one of the ways they get a better understanding of what mortals go through, even if it's not in a compassionate manner.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. Pacts are by far more efficient and less Compromising. The idea for Miracle was for more immediate relief from Conditions - if your agent is Frightened, or Sick, you might need them operational <i>now</i>, not after you've had time for a quick contract. Pacts also only cover Persistent Conditions and Tilts, while this can remove more transitory ones. It can also be used offensively to strip beneficial Conditions like Informed. Not all miracles are beneficial.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=883850#post883850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Banish sounds like it should be temporary, even with an Exceptional Success. The Demon could specify that a group of people are protected (no need to limit the group's size by Primum, just use ST fiat), while others can be affected by the Tilt in a surprise tactic, like how Moses parted the Red Sea and then closed it to drown the Egyptians once the Israelites had crossed. We already have Exploits with names like Sermon, Affliction and Rain Of Blood, so why not go ahead and call this one Parting The Red Sea?</div> </div> </div> </div>Banish is meant for more: the area is on fire (Inferno Tilt), let's remove that for a bit so we don't fry. If the surrounding area is still burning, it will restart once Banish expires. Again, it's more about temporary breathing room.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=883850#post883850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like your maneuvers for Phoenix Pattern, except the last one. I know you tried to live up to the Style's name, but Going Loud and keeping even a partial Cover sounds like having your cake and eating it. It also takes away the incentive for Demons to build burner Covers in case they need to Go Loud, thus opening another way to investigate them. It occurred to me that a Style that improves Going Loud and one for optimizing the regular Demonic Form should be separate. They are quite distinct conceptually: the first is about sheer power, but the other is more about minimizing the risks of Aetheric Resonance/Compromise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cover reclamation was actually the whole point, but I've wrestled with how useful to make it. I might cap the reformed Cover at the level of the &quot;spent&quot; Cover or Primum, whichever is lower - that way you can't shred a burner Cover and get more than you spent. Another option is giving you Cover <i>Experiences</i>, instead of full Dots (meaning at most you can whip up a Cover 3 Patch-Job post throw-down). The idea is to make Going Loud a bit more attractive as an option, especially for higher Primum Demons who get <i>less</i> benefit from it as they grow in power. Going Loud still inflicts a fairly major Glitch, and leaves you Hunted for at least a bit of time (so you aren't just Going Loud to win arguments). And even with this as stated, you are losing any Cover-dependent Merits, since you are making a <i>new</i> Cover after losing the one you burned.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T10:05:19-07:00","id":883871,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>: These are all good points, especially regarding Phoenix Pattern. Losing Cover-related Merits, major/catastrophic Glitches and being Hunted are all serious drawbacks. I don't know how to make the last maneuver more balanced yet attractive, but you seem to be headed in the right direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T12:43:00-07:00","id":889292,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8180\" data-vbnamecard=\"8180\">Deionscribe</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a> I've updated <u>Finders, Keepers</u>, <u>Miracle</u>, and <u>Banish</u>. Still uncertain to modify or just drop Forge the Legend.<br /> <br /> GibberingEloquence: I've also updated Phoenix Pattern <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=881817#post881817\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T16:49:49-07:00","id":889461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=889292#post889292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8180\" data-vbnamecard=\"8180\">Deionscribe</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a> I've updated <u>Finders, Keepers</u>, <u>Miracle</u>, and <u>Banish</u>. Still uncertain to modify or just drop Forge the Legend.<br /> <br /> GibberingEloquence: I've also updated Phoenix Pattern <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=881817#post881817\">here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure how Finders, Keepers is different, but it still looks pretty good to me. I'll probably get to work setting up a GDoc when I got enough time. The semester's almost ending for me.<br /> <br /> Regarding Miracle, it's a pretty interesting (and potent) power. Not surprising, seeing as it's an Exploit. And I can definitely see a Demon using this as either a rush job, or as a way to really demonstrate his power to someone who needs proof that he's the genuine article. Banish, too, is similarly dramatic, though I'm guessing the aforementioned flames and water still remain present despite having no mechanical effect on the character?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T21:18:03-07:00","id":889624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=889461#post889461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure how Finders, Keepers is different, but it still looks pretty good to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I clarified the example stating that points absorbed are capped at successes, for both Success and Exceptional Success. No real change, other than that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=889461#post889461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll probably get to work setting up a GDoc when I got enough time. The semester's almost ending for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=889461#post889461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Miracle, it's a pretty interesting (and potent) power. Not surprising, seeing as it's an Exploit. And I can definitely see a Demon using this as either a rush job, or as a way to really demonstrate his power to someone who needs proof that he's the genuine article. Banish, too, is similarly dramatic, though I'm guessing the aforementioned flames and water still remain present despite having no mechanical effect on the character?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe? Depends how the ST wants to run it. Mechanically, Banish serves to give a Demon breathing room or demonstrate power. Earthquake (as the Tilt) going on? The Demon can waive their hand and create an island of calm. It also allows them to flip the bird at Beasts trying to impose their Lair Traits (provided the Demon wins the Clash of Wills).<br /> <br /> I really like both, in that they have a fairly simple effect (remove Condition or Tilt), that interacts with the game for a diverse range of outcomes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T09:54:58-07:00","id":901095,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Supply and Demand (Mundane)</b></u><br /> <br /> In their previous existences as angels, Psychopomps often required an intimate knowledge of the flows of the resources and commodities that their Infrastructure demanded. This Embed calls upon the vestiges of that ability, allowing the demon to extrapolate from an object's current location and interactions with the world around it where it came from and where it's going.<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Wits + Investigation<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Roll Results:</b><br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The demon not only fails to divine the origins or destination of the object he is examining, he disconnects himself with the flow of causality, imposing a -3 penalty to all rolls involving precision, such as called shots in combat, lockpicking and so on.<br /> <u>Failure:</u> The demon fails to divine the object's origins or destination. He may try again with a cumulative -1 penalty for every failed attempt.<br /> <u>Success:</u> The demon touches and object and receives instinctive knowledge of <i>either</i> its intended next destination or its last destination. This will only reveal where it is intended to go and will not predict accidents or unplanned detours. If it is not intended to move, the demon will feel only its last destination. This Embed can function on living creatures, but is unreliable in such a case, as the living will often change their minds about where they are going.<br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> The demon knows both the object's last destination and its coming one.<br /> <br /> There's going to be an Exploit or two to complement this one coming soon, as well as possibly another Embed. I'm trying to do stuff based around the flows of the world, of both commodities and more esoteric things like ley lines, <i>feng shui</i> esque what-have-yous and so on.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T01:38:42-07:00","id":901877,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u><b>Rivers of Gold</b></u></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">The whole world is in motion. From the orbits of electrons to the movements of humans to the turning of the celestial clockworks, nothing is without motion or energy. Even the occult energies that the God-Machine manipulates as a matter of course move on their own, forming flows and rivers across the world. A demon with the correct knowledge and insight can manipulate such subtle flows and thus control the movements of more earthly things. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Example Prerequisites: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Supply and Demand, Raw Materials</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Dice Pool: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Intelligence + Occult + Primum</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>Action: E</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">xtended (1 day per roll)</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Cost: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">1 Aether/roll</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Roll Results:</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u>Dramatic Failure: </u></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">The demon loses all successes accumulated so far and cannot attempt to use this Exploit on the same thing again for another (11-Primum) weeks. Furthermore, he must roll for Compromise at a -2 penalty as the God-Machine notices his manipulations of the world.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u>Failure: </u></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">The demon accrues no more successes towards his goal. He may either abandon the attempt or gain the Flagged Condition.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u>Success: </u></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">You accrue successes towards your goal.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">This Exploit can be targeted at any 'flow' of commodities, whether that be water (a river), food, jewellery, people, ley lines or anything else, provided that the flow is ongoing (it won't work on a singular delivery). Essentially, this Exploit allows the demon to create a kind of pseudo-Cover in order to change the course or destination of the flow. For example, the demon could cause a regular pizza delivery to a Wal-Mart to always drop off a few boxes on a particular street corner or divert a river so that it no longer supplies cooling water to some of the God-Machine's Infrastructure. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">The number of successes required to divert the flow are adjudicated by the Storyteller, but should be around 3 for a simple, harmless redirection such as the aforementioned pizza van, about 5 for a more involved one such as the river, 7 or so for things like securing a shipment of jewellery every month and 10+ for dealing with beings of the God-Machine or interrupting its Infrastructure. The Machine's metaphysical 'weight' makes it harder to manipulate anything to do with it.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">This Exploit cannot be used to cause the flow to cause damage. In the case of the river, it could not be diverted to flow through a town or a house and nor could the pizza delivery van be caused to crash into that corner. It cannot be used to cause Breaking Points.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Due to the Cover-like properties of the diversion, the only ones who will question the redirection are beings of the God-Machine, other demons or Stigmatics. If the redirection is wildly out of character, like leaving a box of gold on a doorstep, the one making the delivery can roll Resolve + Composure to 'snap out of it'.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u>Exceptional Success:</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"> Extra successes are their own reward. </span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T15:42:49-07:00","id":902330,"title":"","content":"Embed idea <br /> <br /> Title: Watcher Effect<br /> Type: Mundane<br /> <br /> Observation can change how atoms act on a quantum level demons are able to extend this affect to them-self allowing them to sense when there being watched be it by someone on the street or through a sniper scope. This power allows a demon the know when there being observed and from where.<br /> <br /> Dice Pool: Wits + Investigation<br /> <br /> Action: Reflexive, Lasts scene <br /> <br /> Roll Results<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The demon believes there being observed but in the wrong direction and the wrong person and become easier to track by the observer (Thinking maybe some kind of condition)<br /> <br /> Failure: You don't believe your being observed by anyone. <br /> <br /> Success: You can tell your being Observed and which direction the observer is<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: On top of knowing you're being watch and from which direction you also know who the person is and even get a little bit of there intention towards you.<br /> <br /> <br /> Looking for advice on how to make this Embed better <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T07:42:58-07:00","id":904957,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1540_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1540\" data-vbnamecard=\"1540\">Basic</a> I like it. Maybe format it a bit better? Possibly modifications: Let it detect a number of observers per Success. Tells you number, but not direction (until ExS).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T17:26:45-07:00","id":928974,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of these could be worked as Interlocks. That's my go-to if I was playing and wanted to use a homebrew Embed. <br /> <br /> <b>Procrastination:</b> The user can &quot;put off&quot; dealing with something for a time period inversely proportional to severity. So a user about to go bankrupt could make it so that her money doesn't run out until the next day, or someone who was shot could make it so the wound didn't start bleeding or hurting for a turn.<br /> <br /> <b>Confirmation Bias</b>: When the Demon tells someone something and activates it, the person starts seeing evidence in support of whatever the demon said on TV/in magazines/online. So if the Demon says &quot;Don't trust the Deva Corporation&quot;, they'll be flipping through channels and pass a news story about how they polluted a lake. Or they Google &quot;deva corporation&quot; and the top hits are news articles about their shady business practices.<br /> <br /> Exploits:<br /> <br /> <b>Titan's Armory:</b> Temporarily enlarge any weapon held by the user into a larger and more formidable version. Unlike a Gadget, it doesn't gain an Embed or Exploit power and only gains size, durability, and power. However, this power can be used on weapons that are already Gadgets. Ideally meant to be used in Demonic Form: a Gigerian cyberdemon looks a bit silly brandishing a gun or a sword meant for human hands, but this Exploit beefs it up into something more fearsome. This could be a Demonic Form power or Interlock, as well. <br /> <br /> <b>The Land of Morpheus:</b> The Demon can send a target or group of targets into an incredibly advanced and realistic virtual reality simulation that they control, which can be used for a number of purposes: pleasure, interrogation, planning, and training. Not sure if this one could be an Interlock or an Embed. I just really like the idea of Demons being able to create virtual reality spaces. I think I might make the Embed version a separate one called Deep Immersion that causes the target to get so immersed in anything they read/watch/play that it's capable of inflicting Tilts and Conditions on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 07-28-2016, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T11:24:57-07:00","id":938971,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Canary</u> (Mundane)<br /> Time is a flexible concept to the God-Machine. Even many of Its Angels find it more of a suggestion as opposed to an undeniable fact. Consequences of events can echo forward <i>and backwards</i> for those tuned in to see them. A Demon must always be careful not to give signs of themselves away - the most clever look toward potential timelines to avert Compromises that <i>would</i> have happened.<br /> <b>Dice Roll</b>: Wits + </span></span>Subterfuge<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Action</b>: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dramatic Failure</b>: You mistakenly seed the <i>wrong</i> timeline, and pick up false positives at in opportune times. The Storyteller is encouraged to &quot;warn&quot; you of an impending Compromise when it would cause the most paranoia.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Failure</b>: You fail to read temporal currents, but at least you know you need to keep on your toes.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Success</b>: You are able to subtly seed an alarm into your Cover in the future, detecting the telltale ripples cause by Compromise in the past before it occurs. For the rest of the Scene, you are warned of an incoming Compromise check up to 4 minutes (or turns, in combat) before it occurs, though with no information other than a Compromise will be triggered. This is given current circumstances, and the Demon's own actions in the intervening time can (and for most, <i>will</i>) change the predicted outcome.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success</b>: Your alarm also conveys short, applicable context and other data regarding the Compromise check. If it would occur because you are acting out of character rifling through a desk and a guard catches you, you are aware that someone catching you will trigger a Compromise. If you are impersonating someone who always kisses their wife upon first coming in the door, and you were unaware, you would be informed that failing to kiss the person's wife would trigger a Compromise.<br /> <b>Notes</b>: It is up to the Storyteller how descriptive they should be regarding the information conveyed. Some may choose to be stingy with details, to preserve the suspense, while others might simple give a full disclosure just to speed things along. The information is limited to what the Demon can surmise triggered the future Compromise check, however.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Name obviously comes from the whole &quot;Canary in the mine&quot; thing. While a decent alternative to an early warning system when infiltrating, this can also help when you are trying to feel out an improperly researched Cover. It isn't a sure thing, but it helps.]</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T21:26:31-07:00","id":948342,"title":"","content":"Can't remember if this steps on anything's toes. I don't think so. It <i>is</i> kind of the verbal counterpart to Fax.<br /> <br /> <u>Speak of the Demon</u> (AKA Sacred Word, Say My Name, Invoke) (Vocal)<br /> [Desc]<br /> <b>Dice Roll:</b> Wits + Expression<br /> <b>Action:</b> [Instant or Extended?]<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> [Compromise?]<br /> <b>Failure:</b> [Nothing happens, attempt wasted]<br /> <b>Success:</b> [You &quot;flag&quot; one of your &quot;names&quot; for X time. Anyone who speaks it, lets you know their exact location and some general information about them (appearance, how it was spoken).]<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> [The connection is stronger and you are virtually &quot;there&quot; for 1 Turn. Long enough to listen in, glance at the speakers surroundings for more context, or tag them with other Embeds (such as Tag and Release, Across a Crowded Room, etc.)]<br /> <b>Note:</b> The &quot;name&quot; you target is one that both you identify with, and the speaker identifies you with. If they are talking about &quot;John Black&quot; but don't associate it to you, it doesn't trigger. Demons sometimes seed &quot;summoning rituals&quot; with names that have been tagged with the Embed so that they are aware of those seeking Pacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T16:50:58-07:00","id":949629,"title":"","content":"Thinking of this for a embed or interlock but can't think which one it would be better for<br /> <br /> Title: 15 minutes into the future<br /> Type: Mundane<br /> <br /> The Biggest moments in our life all being with subtle shifts in reality. All of these small shifts and actions are to numerous to count by normal human minds but the quantum state of a demon mind allows them to calculate out all of the probable outcomes of a situation when the correct data is inputted. Using this embed a demon can see 15 minutes into the future. Using this power may lead to comprise rolls <br /> <br /> Dice Pool: Wits + Investigation <br /> <br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> <br /> Roll Results<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The demons mind generates a false prediction future events that can lead a demon into a worse situation then there already in be it an immediate danger like getting shot or a danger in the future of an angel finding them. <br /> <br /> Failure: Scrambled future. <br /> <br /> Success: The demon see's the future of everything going on in an area around them equal to Success x Primum yards. The GM gives the player a general description of future events 15 minutes out if they stay the current course. <br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: The demon not only see's the future but can interact with the simulation in there mind by asking the GM what will happen if I do X during this moment. The Player gets Questions equal to there hits <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T22:46:56-07:00","id":950936,"title":"","content":"Are there any Embeds that lets a demon send someone Omens ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T07:20:49-07:00","id":951095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=950936#post950936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any Embeds that lets a demon send someone Omens ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Define Omens? Do you mean abstracted future events?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T13:22:29-07:00","id":951269,"title":"","content":"For example a demon saw the future of someone. They know this person is going to die because of an angel. They don't wanna just insert themselves into the persons life because they would get them flagged. So I was hoping there was a power that allowed demons to send someone omens. To try and change there fate in a low impact way. <br /> <br /> Or they could use it to terrify someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T13:45:56-07:00","id":951291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=951269#post951269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example a demon saw the future of someone. They know this person is going to die because of an angel. They don't wanna just insert themselves into the persons life because they would get them flagged. So I was hoping there was a power that allowed demons to send someone omens. To try and change there fate in a low impact way.<br /> <br /> Or they could use it to terrify someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's basically just a communication power, then. Animal Messenger, Special Message, Across A Crowded Room, etc. would all inform them of what you learned without direct contact.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, if you really wanted to be proactive, use Inflict Stigmata, then Pact with them to gain Omen Sensitivity. They can read Omens themselves, then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T04:28:26-08:00","id":1014699,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Weapon Focus (Instrumental)</b></u><br /> Weapon focus is a psychological phenomenon whereby, in a stressful situation, a person's attention is solely focused on an object - often a weapon. This often causes memories of the rest of the event to become blurred and indistinct. With this Embed, a demon can exploit this tendency, focusing the target's memory on an object on the demon's person - which can be anything - and making it so that, if that person attempts to recall the specifics of the event later, they find it harder. The general gist of the scene is still remembered (e.g. if a robbery took place, that would be recalled). It is only the details, such as what a person looked like or what they were wearing which are obscured. The object which if focused on is remembered with perfect clarity, though.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Persuasion<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Roll Results:</b><br /> <u>Dramatic Failure</u><br /> On a dramatic failure, the target's memory is sharpened to a razor focus, granting them +3 dice if they are called to remember the scene at a later date. Also, if the demon rolls for compromise later in the scene, they suffer a -2 penalty to their roll.<br /> <u>Failure</u><br /> Nothing happens. The demon can try again with a cumulative -1 penalty.<br /> <u>Success</u><br /> The target suffers a penalty to all attempts to precisely recall the scene equal to the demon's successes. If they possess the Eidetic Memory Merit, they suffer no penalty but must still roll.<br /> <u>Exceptional Success</u><br /> More successes are their own reward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 12-09-2016, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T07:39:10-08:00","id":1014763,"title":"","content":"Glad this thread isn't dead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=1014699#post1014699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Weapon Focus (Instrumental)</b></u>...</div> </div> </div> </div>So, despite the name, it works with any object? And the object focus/requirement is why you went Instrumental instead of Mundane (which usually has the &quot;avoid notice&quot; effects)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T08:21:46-08:00","id":1014777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=1014763#post1014763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glad this thread isn't dead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, despite the name, it works with any object? And the object focus/requirement is why you went Instrumental instead of Mundane (which usually has the &quot;avoid notice&quot; effects)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmmhmm. That's right. I'm just editing it now, so that it's an object in the demon's possession which it has to focus on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T14:49:35-07:00","id":1064504,"title":"","content":"Just an idea: Just Scratched<br /> <br /> An embed which allows a demon to perform pretty much any kind of driving stunt and come out with a car/truck/motorbike that's 'just scratched'. Just like the movies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T15:14:37-07:00","id":1064516,"title":"","content":"Catch!<br /> <br /> The demon throws a small object towards someone and on a success they are forced to catch it, dropping whatever they are holding and providing a momentary distraction. On a Dramatic Failure, the demon himself is compelled to catch the object, possibly even diving to the floor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T15:33:46-07:00","id":1064528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=1064504#post1064504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just an idea: Just Scratched<br /> <br /> An embed which allows a demon to perform pretty much any kind of driving stunt and come out with a car/truck/motorbike that's 'just scratched'. Just like the movies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just Bruised Embed does that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-18-2017, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T16:40:29-07:00","id":1064556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=1064528#post1064528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just Bruised Embed does that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Sorry about that. I thought it only applied to the demon themselves, not a vehicle or other stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T18:00:11-07:00","id":1064577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=1064556#post1064556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah. Sorry about that. I thought it only applied to the demon themselves, not a vehicle or other stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, you meant against/to other objects? Sounds perfectly in-scope for a Near Field effect, or Interlock.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T14:47:50-07:00","id":1064933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=1064556#post1064556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah. Sorry about that. I thought it only applied to the demon themselves, not a vehicle or other stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>It works on the Demon themselves or other people, though every use in a scene causes it to take a die penalty past the first. Vehicles and objects, though, not so much. That said, Just Like The Movies could work in this case I think...that or an interlock between the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T08:14:29-07:00","id":1066318,"title":"","content":"The Knights of St. Adrian have an Ink that does that as well. Probably worth checking for inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T13:13:14-07:00","id":1079480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=1064933#post1064933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It works on the Demon themselves or other people, though every use in a scene causes it to take a die penalty past the first. Vehicles and objects, though, not so much. That said, Just Like The Movies could work in this case I think...that or an interlock between the two.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10397_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10397\" data-vbnamecard=\"10397\">ajf115</a> What about a more general Embed that lets the Demon treat any object or structure they are in as if it were themselves for the purposes of other powers? It could be combo'd with Just Bruised, or Turn Blade then (and many other powers). I could easily see it as another potential prerequisite Embed for the Exploit Demon Car.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T14:03:55-07:00","id":1079506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=1079480#post1079480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10397_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10397\" data-vbnamecard=\"10397\">ajf115</a> What about a more general Embed that lets the Demon treat any object or structure they are in as if it were themselves for the purposes of other powers? It could be combo'd with Just Bruised, or Turn Blade then (and many other powers). I could easily see it as another potential prerequisite Embed for the Exploit Demon Car.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could work. All Is One?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T14:09:01-07:00","id":1079510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=1079506#post1079506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That could work. All Is One?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sure? Maybe something referencing a person and their toys, or horse and rider?<br /> <br /> On the last note, I'd imagine in the pre-automotive days, it would see use with mounts, just like Demon Car would have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T05:33:48-07:00","id":1115045,"title":"","content":"I love the idea of demons being able to make hellish minions and this exploit is something I thought of for fun. I would be greatful for any feed back on how I can make it better.<br /> <br /> <b>Horror of Hell</b><br /> The fires of hell just don\u2019t destroy but sometimes it creates creatures from the darkest nightmares the universe can imagine. A demon can release the fire of hell that burns with in them to twist and flesh and bring a new horror into the world.<br /> <br /> Example Prerequisites: (Can\u2019t think of any)<br /> Dice Pool: Intelligence + Occult + Primum vs. Stamina or<br /> Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Cost: Aether = to the Horrors Potency<br /> Roll Results<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The subject is not only burned by the fires of hell but the demons cover is burned by the fires also corrupting their cover. The Demon Gets 1 Permanent CA strophic Glitch of the GM\u2019s Choosing. The Subject is turned into a random horror of a random potency and theme.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The target is not afflicted.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The fires of hell corrupt the subject. The Demon has can give a general idea of what they are trying to create but the process random. For Example, the demon can be looking to create a Succubus from classic myth. The horror could them come out just as they image or more than likely a creature of lust who eats away the sexual drives of everyone around them rather than making everyone becoming more lustful.<br /> <br /> This Exploit does not, however, impart any particular inclination to serve the demon or the God Machine; that inclination must come naturally.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Demon has complete control over what the horror becomes. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T09:13:41-07:00","id":1115109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=1115045#post1115045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the idea of demons being able to make hellish minions and this exploit is something I thought of for fun. I would be greatful for any feed back on how I can make it better.<br /> <br /> <b>Horror of Hell</b><br /> The fires of hell just don\u2019t destroy but sometimes it creates creatures from the darkest nightmares the universe can imagine. A demon can release the fire of hell that burns with in them to twist and flesh and bring a new horror into the world.<br /> <br /> Example Prerequisites: (Can\u2019t think of any)<br /> Dice Pool: Intelligence + Occult + Primum vs. Stamina or<br /> Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Cost: Aether = to the Horrors Potency<br /> Roll Results<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The subject is not only burned by the fires of hell but the demons cover is burned by the fires also corrupting their cover. The Demon Gets 1 Permanent CA strophic Glitch of the GM\u2019s Choosing. The Subject is turned into a random horror of a random potency and theme.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The target is not afflicted.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The fires of hell corrupt the subject. The Demon has can give a general idea of what they are trying to create but the process random. For Example, the demon can be looking to create a Succubus from classic myth. The horror could them come out just as they image or more than likely a creature of lust who eats away the sexual drives of everyone around them rather than making everyone becoming more lustful.<br /> <br /> This Exploit does not, however, impart any particular inclination to serve the demon or the God Machine; that inclination must come naturally.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Demon has complete control over what the horror becomes. </div> </div> </div> </div>You just rewrote the Core Hellhounds Exploit. This power already exists. It creates Cryptids (basically Horrors), though their Aether dependency renders the easier to control.<br /> <br /> Also, Unchained are seeking Hell, so I'm not sure where the Fires of Hell (which Demon's Hell?) Are coming from.<br /> <br /> Sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-12-2017, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T10:41:12-07:00","id":1115136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=1115109#post1115109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You just rewrote the Core Hellhounds Exploit. This power already exists. It creates Cryptids (basically Horrors), though their Aether dependency renders the easier to control.<br /> <br /> Also, Unchained are seeking Hell, so I'm not sure where the First of Hell (which Demon's Hell?) Are coming from.<br /> <br /> Sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh I forgot about that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T00:35:31-07:00","id":1118430,"title":"","content":"This is an exploit I've been pondering on for a while, partially for gadgets, partially because I've not found an Exploit that can do something like this. I'm not sure how balanced it is, but I'm definitely open to critique on it.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Compression Elimination</b></u><br /> Molecules are the building blocks of life, set in all kinds of patterns that give various properties to the substances they compose. The God-Machine has long since learned how to manipulate them in strange ways, not the least of which reducing the distance between these molecules. Demons, meanwhile, have learned how not only how to use this process but how to reverse it.<br /> <br /> This exploit may be used on people, inanimate objects and animals, including other Unchained. The size difference is small but, as the saying goes, every inch helps.<br /> <br /> <b>Example Prerequisites:</b> In My Pocket, Quick Change<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Intelligence + Science + Primum vs. (if contested) Stamina + Supernatural Resistance OR Durability<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2 Aether + 1 to only affect the core target.<br /> <b>Roll Results:</b><br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> Rather than feeling crushed, the target feels invigorated, stronger than ever, their entire being fortified. The target gains two dots of Armor as their molecular structure , as well as a +1 bonus to any rolls requiring Strength. This effect lasts a<br /> <u>Failure:</u> The target remains their current size.<br /> <u>Success:</u> The target is subjected to a brief glow, before a crushing sensation comes over them. The Demon selects one of the results below. If the target is garbed, the Demon may pay an additional Aether to only affect the core target itself. A package may strip its wrapping, while a guard may find herself tripping over her own uniform; if the garb is inflexible, it may cause the target some harm. The exploit lasts for the scene, although the Demon can end the effect early.<br /> <b>* Expansion:</b> The target expands to a new size, gaining 1 Size. If the target is a living being, they gain the benefits (and detriments) of the Giant merit for the duration of the exploit. If the target is an inanimate object, it gains 1 Durability, adding 2 to the object\u2019s Structure; a melee weapon may gain a +1 modifier to its damage. When the target returns to their normal size, if the temporary health box has damage, upgrade the leftmost health box as though the target had taken new damage (this cannot be mitigated by merits).<br /> <b>* Compression:</b> The target compresses, losing 1 Size. If the target is a living being, they lose their rightmost healthbox for the duration of the exploit but gain the benefits (and pitfalls) of the Small Framed merit. Any damage within that health box remains when the target returns to full size. If the target is an inanimate object, it loses 1 Structure, minimum 1.<br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u><br /> The Demon finds a quantum sweet spot, allowing them to be more selective with their changes.<br /> * The target is penalized by -2 for Athletics or Brawl rolls as their limbs are made too large or small to effectively use. Alternatively, the target suffers the Arm or Leg Wrack tilt, their limbs painfully crushed or bloated around their skeleton. Notably, this cannot target organs nor break bones.<br /> * The Demon may pay an additional three aether to permanently alter the target\u2019s entire size, effectively granting (or removing) the Giant or Small Framed merit. This effect may only be applied to a normal Success result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T02:30:36-07:00","id":1118460,"title":"","content":"So, like the Collapsible and Huge Size Form Abilities, but external and downgraded? Nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T08:18:24-07:00","id":1118564,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> More or less. I was looking for the utility of the form powers for gadgets, but I didn't want to make the powers themselves redundant. I'm not entirely sure about the exceptional success effect that permanently alters the target though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T05:36:32-07:00","id":1119848,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Follow the Leader (Vocal)</b></u><br /> People are herd animals inclined to go alone with the group or an authority figure. This Embed reinforces that drive and designates who the authority figure is. The Demon activates this Embed after the primary target takes an action. Each target lower in the Initiative order who fails to resist copies the primary target's action (exactly, if applicable) for their own this turn.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Politics vs Composure<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Roll Result</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b>: All secondary targets in range do whatever the Demon <i>doesn't</i> want.<br /> <b>Failure</b>: Those unaffected continue to do whatever they decide would be best.<br /> <b>Success</b>: Secondary targets that don't resist duplicate the same action as the primary target for their action that turn.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: The Demon can grant either the Inspired (as they rally around the decisive leadership), or the Disoriented (representing confusion and broken command structure) Condition to the secondary targets, albeit it fades without Resolution after one Turn.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: This is for spreading out actions, such as if one enemy attacks the wrong target, getting their buddies to do so too, or triggering mass retreat, or conscripting back to the Demon's own actions.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-27-2017, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T16:37:56-07:00","id":1148467,"title":"","content":"<u><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Brimstone With Treacle (Instrumental)</span></span></u><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To the God-Machine, changing matter from one substance to another is child\u2019s play, both on a small and a large scale. Though it takes Demons far more effort to do anything close to that, some have found liquids to be easier to influence. This embed can only be used on liquids that are contained in some way, without anything entering or leaving the vessel, and on less than a liter in volume. The Demon must touch the vessel, or the liquid itself, before activating the embed. If the liquid being changed has few if any impurities, the storyteller may evoke a -2 penalty to the activation of the embed.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Science</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Action:</b> Standard</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Roll Results:</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The liquid becomes into foul, bubbling sludge, not unlike molasses in consistency. Treat the liquid as having a toxicity rating equal to half the Demon\u2019s Primum (rounded down), should anyone try to drink it. An hour after forming, the sludge hardens into a brittle, smelly lump.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Failure: </b>The beverage remains the same; the Demon may try again in the same turn with a -1 penalty.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Success:</b> The liquid changes, various impurities being transformed into another substance. However, the Demon cannot make anything new in the liquid - she is only reducing the ratio of different substances. If the Demon is aware of a particular impurity, be it a chemical, poison or simply a flavoring they don\u2019t enjoy, they can target that solely and reduce or increase its level (or toxicity rating) up to their activation successes. Cheeky Demons are known to induce carbonation this way.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Demon has far greater control over the beverage than they would otherwise, allowing them to change its contents entirely. Whether the liquid is spring water or crude oil, the Demon may make it into wine, honey, or even lace a previously safe drink with a drug or poison with a toxicity rating up to half their Primum (rounded down). A Demon with a catastrophic glitch may also use this opportunity to create a drink they are otherwise only able to consume, such as motor oil or battery acid. However, a Demon must be careful when using this effect, as the drink will visibly change color and opacity if the changes are overt.<br /> [Comment: This is one I've been pondering on for a bit. The name is from the Mary Poppins stage show, the song &quot;Brimstone and Treacle&quot; - it gave me a lot of imagery for the eventual version of the embed here.]</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T03:09:54-07:00","id":1149355,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Little Drop of Poison </b></u><br /> In the spy game you have to watch out for poisons, drugs and so on. A demon with this embed cause his body to burn through drugs and poisons before they can do real harm to their cover.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Science or Med Action: Reflex Roll Results<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b>: The drug or poisons effect takes a stronger hold on the user rising its effect by the 2x<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> Poison or drug takes effect<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> Drug or Poison takes no effect<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> As Above, plus you now become immune to that drug or poison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T14:39:18-07:00","id":1150785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=1149355#post1149355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Little Drop of Poison </b></u><br /> In the spy game you have to watch out for poisons, drugs and so on. A demon with this embed cause his body to burn through drugs and poisons before they can do real harm to their cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I like the idea of this Embed, I feel it's a tad too potent as is. It outright removes risk from a lot of scenarios, and while the Embed can fail it still grants instant relief and in the thick of combat.<br /> <br /> My suggestion would be to make the Success effect &quot;Reduce the toxicity of a drug or poison in the Demon's system up to the Demon's activation successes; if there are multiple toxins, the Demon may split these successes to reduce each one individually. If the drug or poison is based on supernatural origins or methods, or is causing a supernatural effect, it evokes a Clash of Wills.&quot; This gives a bit more finesse to the Embed, especially if a Demon wants to only reduce a toxin in their system rather than outright remove it, but it doesn't prevent a Demon from using the Embed multiple times to clear the effect if they're not too bothered by it. It also gives some stress during combat, if a character is being actively poisoned by the enemy. This also applies to something like Vampire blood, which is like a drug but supernatural in origin.<br /> <br /> For an Exceptional Success, I'd go a slightly different route; &quot;The Demon purges their system of any drugs or poisons inhabiting it, no matter how strong. If the Demon only had a single toxin running through them, they may also take the Toxic Resistance Condition (read below).&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Toxic Resistance</b><br /> The human body has a habit of developing immunities to various toxins that manage to infiltrate it. Demons simply managed to find a way to expedite the process. Whenever the character is dosed with a particular drug or poison, treat the Toxicity rating as one lower than it normally would be. If the toxicity rating becomes zero, the character is immune to it. The character may have multiple versions of this condition, each for a specific drug or poison.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Shed this condition to become completely immune to the toxin for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> The reason I go for a condition instead of immunity for the scene (or outright immunity) is that I think it offers a bit more utility for the Demon without being too overpowered, while still allowing them a brief time of immunity should they need it. That said, I'm not sure if making a lingering effect is entirely appropriate for an Embed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T04:00:32-07:00","id":1153106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=1150785#post1150785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I like the idea of this Embed, I feel it's a tad too potent as is. It outright removes risk from a lot of scenarios, and while the Embed can fail it still grants instant relief and in the thick of combat.<br /> <br /> My suggestion would be to make the Success effect &quot;Reduce the toxicity of a drug or poison in the Demon's system up to the Demon's activation successes; if there are multiple toxins, the Demon may split these successes to reduce each one individually. If the drug or poison is based on supernatural origins or methods, or is causing a supernatural effect, it evokes a Clash of Wills.&quot; This gives a bit more finesse to the Embed, especially if a Demon wants to only reduce a toxin in their system rather than outright remove it, but it doesn't prevent a Demon from using the Embed multiple times to clear the effect if they're not too bothered by it. It also gives some stress during combat, if a character is being actively poisoned by the enemy. This also applies to something like Vampire blood, which is like a drug but supernatural in origin.<br /> <br /> For an Exceptional Success, I'd go a slightly different route; &quot;The Demon purges their system of any drugs or poisons inhabiting it, no matter how strong. If the Demon only had a single toxin running through them, they may also take the Toxic Resistance Condition (read below).&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Toxic Resistance</b><br /> The human body has a habit of developing immunities to various toxins that manage to infiltrate it. Demons simply managed to find a way to expedite the process. Whenever the character is dosed with a particular drug or poison, treat the Toxicity rating as one lower than it normally would be. If the toxicity rating becomes zero, the character is immune to it. The character may have multiple versions of this condition, each for a specific drug or poison.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Shed this condition to become completely immune to the toxin for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> The reason I go for a condition instead of immunity for the scene (or outright immunity) is that I think it offers a bit more utility for the Demon without being too overpowered, while still allowing them a brief time of immunity should they need it. That said, I'm not sure if making a lingering effect is entirely appropriate for an Embed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Think about it like this. If that is too powerful then why not make it months equal too primum you're immuned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T05:04:58-07:00","id":1153123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=1153106#post1153106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Think about it like this. If that is too powerful then why not make it months equal too primum you're immuned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Embeds generally don't (and shouldn't) interact with Primum.<br /> <br /> Nor should their effects be long lasting without consequence. If you want something that scales with Primum and grants outright immunity, why not make it an Exploit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T11:11:01-07:00","id":1153228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=1153123#post1153123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Embeds generally don't (and shouldn't) interact with Primum.<br /> <br /> Nor should their effects be long lasting without consequence. If you want something that scales with Primum and grants outright immunity, why not make it an Exploit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, some Embeds do interact with Primum, but it usually acts as a safe limit rather than a positive one - In My Pocket or Victory At Any Price, for example, limit their uses per session/scene up to the user's Primum, after which any use evokes a compromise roll.<br /> <br /> Still, that is a fair point. Makes me wonder if perhaps my condition idea is a little too potent in and of itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=1153106#post1153106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Think about it like this. If that is too powerful then why not make it months equal too primum you're immuned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside from Vent0's point, it also makes your Embed redundant for that game time, and if a Demon has enough dice to get exceptional sucesses relatively easily, then doesn't that require raised stakes so that they don't just start strolling through areas humans otherwise can't go? Not to mention you can make a number of mean gadgets with something that, by default, grants immunity to drugs and toxins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T05:25:27-07:00","id":1153441,"title":"","content":"How about <i>delaying</i> the poison from taking effect for the period? Like a success gives you a few minutes and an exceptional gives you an hour, or something along those lines? It's still niche, but it doesn't outright grant you immunity, but it gives you a measure of control of when you're going to suffer for it. So you can be poisoned or whatever, but you'll suffer no ill effects for a bit and have time to get to your secret car medkit or whatever, which is its own spy trope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T14:07:31-07:00","id":1153583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=1153441#post1153441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about <i>delaying</i> the poison from taking effect for the period? Like a success gives you a few minutes and an exceptional gives you an hour, or something along those lines? It's still niche, but it doesn't outright grant you immunity, but it gives you a measure of control of when you're going to suffer for it. So you can be poisoned or whatever, but you'll suffer no ill effects for a bit and have time to get to your secret car medkit or whatever, which is its own spy trope.</div> </div> </div> </div>That feels like a bit too far of a step back. I like the idea of neutralizing poison, considering we have Embeds that grant 8-again to particular rolls, new dots in skills, completely new items from pockets and even a free success on a roll, but outright immunity on a single success sounds too far. Maybe the neutralizing aspect should be for exceptional success, delaying poison for the scene for a normal success?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T21:45:41-07:00","id":1154612,"title":"","content":"Stub:<br /> <br /> <u>Contingency Plan</u><br /> A careful Demon learns to plan for everything. By bending time and Causality, the Unchained can suspend an action in time until conditions are met, activating without any further input needed. The Demon must declare the action they will take and the condition that will trigger it, and once that exact criteria is met, the stated action triggers immediately.<br /> <i>Example: </i><br /> <b>Example Prerequisites</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: </span></span>Cause and Effect, Wait For It<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Intelligence + Computers + Primum<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant + triggered action<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3 Aether<br /> <b>Roll Result</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The triggered action goes off now instead of when relied upon.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The triggered actions fails to set, but the Demon can try again.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The preset effect goes off right Reflexively after the triggering condition is fulfilled. [Costs must be paid at that point in time.]<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Demon can choose whether the triggered action will go off or not each time the condition comes up, preventing accidental or deliberate misfires.<br /> <b>Possible Modifiers:</b> -2 for day long duration, -4 for week long duration, -6 for month long duration, -8 for year long duration.<br /> <b>Special:</b> A Demon can only have a number of Contingency Plans active at once equal to their Primum.<br /> [<u>Comments:</u> ]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-01-2017, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T03:38:28-07:00","id":1154662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=1154612#post1154612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stub:<br /> <br /> Contingency Plan<br /> A careful Demon learns to plan for everything. By bending time and Causality, the Unchained can suspend an action in time until right (before?) conditions are met. The Demon must declare the action they will take and the condition that will trigger it, and once that exact criteria is met, the stated action triggers immediately (before?) without any input by the Demon required.<br /> Dice Pool: Intelligence + __ + Primum - __<br /> Roll Result<br /> DF<br /> F<br /> S: The preset effect goes off right before the set trigger.<br /> ES: Same as S, but can stack? Decide to activate or not?<br /> Special: A Demon can only have a number of Contingency Plans active at once equal to their Primum.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This sounds like a story telling function already in the book. It allows players to say we already did x y z before hand because demons can think a head. I think they said its like burn notice or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T04:42:22-07:00","id":1154667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=1154662#post1154662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This sounds like a story telling function already in the book. It allows players to say we already did x y z before hand because demons can think a head. I think they said its like burn notice or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, this is a mechanics specific effect similar to the Contingency spell in D&amp;D - whenever X happens, then Y happens automatically.<br /> <br /> Examples: <br /> When I notice an Angel, Then trigger Going Native.<br /> When my last Health box is filled with Lethal damage, Go Loud.<br /> When my Plan fails, Then trigger 4 Minutes Ago.<br /> <br /> You state X, then Y happens Reflexively. I'm just unsure when to check for the 2ndary effect (at setup, or at activation), and whether to stipulate Y must occur before, or after.<br /> <br /> Since the Exploit isn't permanent (without cost or limit?), keeping a stable of Contingency Plans active all the time will be expensive in both Aether and Compromise checks. But it does allow a Demon to trigger a specific action even if otherwise incapacitated.<br /> <br /> You might be able to achieve the same results with Gadget triggers, depending on the ST, but this is explicit.<br /> <br /> I am concerned about Action-Economy-Breaking Contingency-Chains, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-01-2017, 07:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T01:03:36-07:00","id":1225830,"title":"","content":"<u>Lifeline</u><br /> Life is a beautiful thing, and often too short for what one wants to experience. For Demons, even with their true form being effectively immortal, life truly is too short. However, though Demons may not be able to raise themselves or their Unchained brethren with any form of ease, they can link onto someone else\u2019s life to avoid death for a short time. Only one link may be established at a time.<br /> <br /> <b>Example Prerequisites:</b> Remote Linkup, Just Bruised<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Strength + Medicine + Primum Vs Resolve + Primum (if contested)<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3 Aether if Contested; 2 Aether if welcomed<br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> A black line briefly forms between the Demon and her target, but instead of life being linked it is sickliness. Both the target and the Demon take two Lethal damage and the Sick tilt before the line suddenly snaps.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The line fails to form. However, the Demon may try again.<br /> <b>Success:</b> A golden line briefly links the Demon and her target, and splits into a gold bangle around each of their wrists. Whenever one of the linked parties would take damage, it is halved and applied to both the linked parties; if the damage cannot be split evenly, the original target takes the spare damage. If one of the linked parties has their last health box filled with Aggravated damage, they do not die. However, any damage they accrue is transferred in full to the linked party; this includes degrading health from Aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> With this power, a dying Demon could take her assailant down with her, take another person hostage in a dangerous scenario or even to outright save someone else's life until medical treatments can be administered. However, if the lifeline expires while one of the parties' health is full of Aggravated damage, the target immediately dies. The exploit lasts until the end of the scene or until both parties exceed (10 x Primum) yards from another, the bangles dimming with time and distance.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Demon may either have the link remain indefinitely, provided the linked parties remain in range, OR may have the link only go in one direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 06-08-2018, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-23T03:08:58-07:00","id":1248828,"title":"","content":"(Full version below, now that the forum is fixed)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-15-2018, 06:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-23T03:24:08-07:00","id":1248831,"title":"","content":"<u>Everything Is Fine (Mundane)</u><br /> Humanity possesses a seemingly limitless capacity for self-delusion, able to tolerate and justify whatever circumstances they need to so they can continue their routine. A Demon can manually activate this inclination, arresting mental shock... for a time.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Subterfuge - Wits<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Demon instead warps the Target's perceptions, triggering a Breaking Point. Regardless of current circumstances, they suspect the Demon is somehow responsible.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The Demon's manipulations are unable to overcome the Target's own reactions. Breaking Points are incurred normally.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The target can ignore one source or category of Breaking Points for 4 days, acting as if nothing exceptional occurred that they need to think deeply about or get agitated over had happened. At the end, however, if they still retain the memory of the events, they must make all deferred Breaking Points (at their current modifiers), at one per Scene until finished.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Demon can blind a person's reaction to <i>anything</i> that would disturb them, or make their justifications particularly enduring. You can choose to either entirely prevent Breaking Points for the duration, or eliminate the need to roll any incurred at the end.<br /> <b>Note:</b> At the Storyteller's discretion, this may work on certain supernaturals' Integrity equivalents (such as Humanity or Pilgrimage), provided they result from the being's own reaction to events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-15-2018, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T11:12:41-07:00","id":1254261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=1248831#post1248831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for the near-double post - I seem to be unable to get the edit saved (from my phone) and the text entry is blocked on my PC over what appears to be security certificate issues.<br /> <br /> Here is the edited version, with dice pool.<br /> <br /> <u>Everything Is Fine (Mundane)</u><br /> Humanity possesses a seemingly limitless capacity for self-delusion, able to tolerate and justify whatever circumstances they need to so they can continue their routine. A Demon can manually activate this inclination, arresting mental shock... for a time.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Subterfuge - Wits<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Demon instead warps the Target's perceptions, triggering a Breaking Point. Regardless of current circumstances, they suspect the Demon is somehow responsible.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The Demon's manipulations are unable to overcome the Target's own reactions. Breaking Points are incurred normally.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The target can ignore one source or category of Breaking Points for 4 days, acting as if nothing exceptional occurred that they need to think deeply about or get agitated over had happened. At the end, however, if they still retain the memory of the events, they must make all deferred Breaking Points (at their current modifiers), at one per Scene until finished.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Demon can blind a person's reaction to <i>anything</i> that would disturb them, or ake their justifications particularly enduring. You can choose to either entirely prevent Breaking Points for the duration, or eliminate the need to roll any incurred at the end.<br /> <b>Note:</b> At the Storyteller's discretion, this may work on certain supernaturals' Integrity equivalents (such as Humanity or Pilgrimage), provided they result from the being's own reaction to events.</div> </div> </div> </div>Change it to hours equal to hits + premium<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T03:16:20-07:00","id":1254437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=1254261#post1254261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Change it to hours equal to hits + premium</div> </div> </div> </div>Trying not to use Primum for Embeds. That way they work better with Demon-blooded.<br /> <br /> As for Successes in Days, that gets obviated by the Exceptional Success (maybe), so it doesn't fully scale. Still as possibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-18-2018, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T03:31:30-07:00","id":1254440,"title":"","content":"<u>No Vacancy</u><br /> You can only fill a glass of water so much before before it can't contain any more. Similarly, a given object or person can only contain so much spiritual power... at least, before it gets strained. By filling the target with Aether, you can block out immaterial invaders from possessing or becoming attached to the subject.<br /> <b>Example Prerequisites:</b> Soup Up, Interference, Seance<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Occult + Primum - Size<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1+ Aether<br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> You've warped the target with demonic power. Maybe it mutates into a Cryptid, becomes a hostile Stigmatic, or simply takes damage equal to the Aether spent.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> You push Aether towards the target, but it doesn't take - if the target has an Aether pool or can serve as a Stockpile, then it absorbs the Aether, but is still subject to ephemeral invasion.<br /> <b>Success:</b> You flood the target's spiritual &quot;ports&quot; with Aether, causing a Clash of Wills toward any attempt to use Manifestations directly upon them (such as Fetter, Possession, or Claim). Each such attempt depletes the amount of Aether spent upon this Exploit by 1 - additionally, 1 point of Aether fades automatically each month, regardless of Manifestation attempts. Once the spend Aether reaches 0, the Exploit ends, but if reused, it can be &quot;topped up&quot; and last indefinitely (which add a +4 to the Clash of Wills for Duration). This Exploit cannot prevent or remove Manifestations already in effect, but can prevent any new ones from being applied.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> You manage to rig the Aether to act not merely as a wall, but as a trap. Each unsuccessful attempt at a Manifestation deals 1 Lethal damage to the Ephemeral attempting it, while a successful attempt deals the <i>remaining</i> Aether in Lethal Damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-18-2018, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-18T15:20:05-07:00","id":1255345,"title":"","content":"Made <u>Everything is Fine</u> and <u>No Vacancy</u> to kinda patch over Soul Loss. Specifically for one Stigmatic Agent I have brewing that uses Form Gadgets. She had a Precision Engineered pair of Gadgets with Everything is Fine (set to block out Breaking Points from pursing her Vice) and No Vacancy.<br /> <br /> No Vacancy also is good for hedging out Ephemerals that Demon's normally don't have much interaction with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-19T05:45:07-07:00","id":1313106,"title":"","content":"<u>Uncertainty Principle (Mundane)</u><br /> Either a particle's current position or momentum can be known. Demons with this Embed have remembered how to apply similar principles to their own metaphysical nature, shrouding either their current position, or future path from occult detection.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Occult<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Demon's attempt to mask their signature backfires and instead alerts the God-Machine as to their presence. Make a Compromise roll.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The detection effect goes through, identifying the Demon's location or interaction in a future event. The Demon is at least aware of this.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The Demon can block the attempt to detect their location, reading as if they do not exist in the area or anywhere in existence. Alternatively, if the effect was attempting to ascertain their Fate or predict their future actions, or involvement in a future event, that reads as if the Demon wasn't present or does nothing.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Demon's manipulations are adroit enough to substitute false information, as well as uncover details about what they are attempting to fabricate - they know who is attempting to locate them, or what future the attempting party is trying to forecast for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T00:59:41-07:00","id":1319416,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u><b>Little Drop Of Poison</b></u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Description:</b> The human body extremely susceptible to various chemicals. The demon using this embed can poison a targets drink by looking at it as long as the drink is not being watched. The demon can also do the same directly to a target by touching them be it with an object or with their body. Example touching a target with your umbrella while walking by them.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Demon with this embed can create poisons to kill, knockout or cause other effects such as hallucinogenic. The demon can also put the poison on a delayed effect</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Medicine</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Action:</b> Instant</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><u>Roll Results:</u></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Poison backfired the poison was so week the person gains resistance to further poison attempts and the demon takes on the poisoned Condition</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Failure:</b> No Effect</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Success:</b> The embed takes effect each hit is the toxicity level of poison and the demon sets the poison roll interval and the effect they're going for, be it to kill the target or just knock them out. The target makes a Stamina + Resolve - Toxicity roll. Each success reduces the damage taken by one. This roll must be made every time the poison deals damage unless the character stops fighting and gives in. The target also takes the Poisoned Condition &quot;moderate&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Exceptional Success:</b> As above but the target now takes Poisoned &quot;Grave.&quot; The poison is now also undetectable or can set it as a type of poison such as anthrax or even a drug overdose</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-18T14:34:33-07:00","id":1331516,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u><b>Here and Gone</b></u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Description:</b> Sometimes guns bombs and another thing just won't work on things like ghosts, spirits or other strange ephemeral beings. This is went demons can use their knowledge of reality to super charge mundane banishing spells.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Occult</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Action:</b> Instant</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><u>Roll Results:</u></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The user of the embed opens a rift, in reality, letting more beings into their world.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Failure:</b> Nothing Happens</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Success:</b> The targeted ephemeral beings are sent back to their plane of existence</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Exceptional Success:</b> The targeted ephemeral being is not only sent back to their plane of existence but is barred from re-entering the characters plane of existence for weeks equal to primum level</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T06:47:57-07:00","id":1389653,"title":"","content":"<u>Bug In The System</u><br /> A Demon's interface with reality isn't as smooth and reliable any more after disconnecting from the God-Machine. Their forms develop irregularities most refer to simply as Glitches. But these are just traits, and like many such traits, can be added to, or even altered on other subjects.<br /> <b>Example Prerequisites:</b> Interference, Cause and Effect, Sabotage<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Occult + Primum - Resolve + Primum<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Aether<br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Demonic ends up breaking their own connection to reality and immediately rolls for a Glitch of their own.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> Lights flicker, clocks run backwards for a few seconds before catching up, and other oddities occur, but no long-term effects happen for the subject.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The target's connection with reality is altered. A target immediately gains a Transient Minor Glitch. These Glitches have a duration based on Successes as if they were Primum, not the target's Primum. More severe Glitches can be inflicted with a penalty determined below.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Demon's hack is particularly deep. In addition to the greater duration due to more effective Primum, the Demon can inflict Emanations as their Glitch.<br /> <b>Possible Modifiers:</b> -2 Glitch is Major, -4 Glitch is Catastrophic, +2 to change a Glitch instead of inflicting a new one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-21-2020, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T18:58:21-07:00","id":1541906,"title":"","content":"<b>Phantom Sniper</b> <i>(Instrumental)</i><br /> <br /> When demons need to create the illusion of an unseen ally or pull off precise, long-range strikes without drawing attention, they use <b>Phantom Sniper</b>. This Embed makes it appear as if a sniper has taken a shot from an unknown location, hitting the demon\u2019s chosen target with lethal or non-lethal force, depending on their intention. Whether the shot knocks a gun out of someone\u2019s hand, incapacitates an enemy, or causes a dramatic injury, this Embed makes it happen with uncanny precision.<br /> <br /> Despite the lethality or precision of the attack, the sound and source of the shot are distant, untraceable, and nearly impossible to locate.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: Wits + Firearms<br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results</b>:<ul><li><b>Dramatic Failure</b>: The shot misfires spectacularly. Either the wrong person is hit, or the shot ricochets, causing unintended damage. The demon immediately risks exposure as the failure is noticeable and dramatic.</li> <li><b>Failure</b>: The shot is fired, but it either misses entirely or does not achieve the desired effect. The target is aware of the attempt, and the environment may still reveal suspicious signs of tampering.</li> <li><b>Success</b>: The demon designates a target within line of sight, and the phantom sniper executes a perfect shot. The shot can either:<ul><li>Inflict lethal damage.</li> <li>Inflict non-lethal damage, incapacitating or disarming the target.</li> <li>Cause a precise effect, such as shooting an object (e.g., knocking a weapon out of a target\u2019s hand or hitting a pressure point for temporary paralysis).<br /> No sound or clear trace of where the shot came from is left behind, and witnesses are left confused about where the shooter might be.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Exceptional Success</b>: The shot hits with pinpoint precision, achieving the demon\u2019s desired effect flawlessly. The phantom sniper feels like a professional sharpshooter on their side. Any witnesses are not only confused but also too unnerved to act, leaving the demon to handle the situation undisturbed.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Additional Effects</b>:<ul><li>The demon can specify whether the phantom sniper shot is lethal or non-lethal before rolling.</li> <li>This Embed leaves no traceable evidence of the source of the attack, making it appear as though a real sniper from an unseen position took the shot.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-20T15:18:09-07:00","id":1552555,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>All Calls Lead to Me</b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Type:</b> Vocal Embed<br /> <br /> <b>Angelic Origin:</b><br /> <i>Messengers tasked with intelligence and counter-intelligence duties were often required to control the flow of information to or from a person of interest. To ensure a target only received God-Machine-approved directives or to prevent sensitive data from leaking, an angel could apply a filter to reality's communication subroutines. From the angel's perspective, it wasn't hijacking anything; it was merely correcting the signal-to-noise ratio to fulfill its mission parameters, ensuring all communication adhered to the divine plan.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Demonic Adaptation:</b><br /> <i>A demon remembers this subroutine for manipulating information flow and turns it into a powerful tool of espionage. By designating a target, the demon can reroute the flow of communication, not to the God-Machine, but directly to themselves. It's an ideal way to isolate an enemy, gather blackmail, impersonate a target's allies, or simply stay one step ahead. On a conceptual level, a clever demon can use this Embed to monopolize a secret, ensuring that whenever a specific topic is discussed, only they receive the true meaning.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>System:</b><br /> The demon can use this Embed in two ways: on a person or on a topic.<br /> <br /> <b>Targeting a Person:</b> The demon redirects a target's outgoing electronic and telephonic communications. This includes phone calls, text messages, emails, and direct messages on social media. It does not affect face-to-face conversations or physical letters. The demon must have seen the target in person to establish the connection, but the Embed works regardless of distance once active.<br /> <br /> <b>Targeting a Topic:</b> The demon chooses a specific topic of conversation (e.g., &quot;the location of the safe house,&quot; &quot;Project Chimera,&quot; &quot;the demon's true identity&quot;). For the rest of the scene, any attempts by others to communicate about that specific topic are misheard or misinterpreted by everyone except the demon, who hears the intended words perfectly. To all other listeners, the words are twisted into bland, forgettable chatter.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Computers vs Resolve (if targeting a person) or highest Composure present (if targeting a topic)<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Embed backfires spectacularly. The demon's own incoming and outgoing communications are randomly scrambled and misdirected for the next 24 hours. The player must make a compromise roll at a -2 penalty.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> The Embed fails to take hold. The demon may try again on the same target or topic, but suffers a cumulative -1 penalty for each attempt in the same scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The Embed activates.<ul><li><b>On a Person:</b> For the next 24 hours, all the target's specified communications are redirected to the demon. The target receives a false confirmation (a &quot;sent&quot; receipt, a normal-sounding dial tone before the call is rerouted) and believes their messages are going through. The demon may spend successes to increase the duration by one day per success spent.</li> <li><b>On a Topic:</b> For the rest of the scene, the demon is the only one who can understand when the chosen topic is discussed.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The effect is more potent.<ul><li><b>On a Person:</b> As success, and the deception becomes flawless. The demon can now send replies that appear to come from the target's intended recipients. The target receives these spoofed messages and has no reason to believe they aren't genuine.</li> <li><b>On a Topic:</b> As success, and the effect lasts for 24 hours instead of one scene.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}